WEBVTT

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:08.142 line:80%
[♪ theme music playing]

00:00:33.959 --> 00:00:35.002 line:80%
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

00:00:38.088 --> 00:00:39.631 line:80%
CHARACTERS, EVENTS, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND PLACES IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

00:00:39.715 --> 00:00:41.008 line:80%
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

00:00:42.634 --> 00:00:44.178 line:80%
Then is it okay if I like you?

00:00:44.762 --> 00:00:46.597 line:80%
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

00:00:47.681 --> 00:00:49.600 line:80%
[stammers]

00:00:52.394 --> 00:00:55.230 line:80%
[heartbeats echoing]

00:01:07.743 --> 00:01:08.869 line:80%
Uh…

00:01:08.952 --> 00:01:12.164 line:80%
-I think we should turn this off.
-[clicks]

00:01:13.749 --> 00:01:16.710 line:80%
[stutters] I didn't mean that…

00:01:16.794 --> 00:01:19.171 line:80%
I didn't mean that, either.

00:01:19.254 --> 00:01:23.050 line:80%
My grandmother kept talking
about us dating,

00:01:24.218 --> 00:01:25.511 line:80%
so I was just…

00:01:26.345 --> 00:01:29.890 line:80%
trying to stop that in advance
since you might feel uneasy.

00:01:30.474 --> 00:01:31.475 line:80%
That's all.

00:01:32.059 --> 00:01:33.811 line:80%
That's really it?

00:01:35.521 --> 00:01:36.855 line:80%
[mumbles]

00:01:39.358 --> 00:01:40.776 line:80%
Should there be something else?

00:01:43.153 --> 00:01:44.446 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:45.990 line:80%
I'll start driving, then.

00:01:50.202 --> 00:01:51.203 line:20%
EPISODE 5

00:01:51.286 --> 00:01:52.287 line:20%
GYEONGJU

00:01:52.371 --> 00:01:55.582 line:20%
[reporter over radio] <i>The cold is expected</i>
<i>to arrive earlier this year than usual.</i>

00:01:55.666 --> 00:01:59.378 line:20%
<i>The first snow may fall sooner</i>
<i>than average as well.</i>

00:01:59.461 --> 00:02:01.463 line:20%
<i>The continental high-pressure system--</i>

00:02:05.509 --> 00:02:06.510 line:20%
[Chan sighs]

00:02:08.095 --> 00:02:10.139 line:20%
It would be a shame to just leave.

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:13.309 line:20%
Can you pull over?

00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:18.272 line:20%
[water gushing]

00:02:20.149 --> 00:02:21.692 line:20%
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

00:02:25.612 --> 00:02:29.116 line:80%
Wow. It would've been a huge shame
if we'd just left.

00:02:33.996 --> 00:02:34.997 line:80%
I hate snow.

00:02:36.206 --> 00:02:37.750 line:80%
Especially the first snow.

00:02:39.209 --> 00:02:40.502 line:80%
The first snow?

00:02:40.586 --> 00:02:42.588 line:80%
Remember what I told you about my parents?

00:02:43.172 --> 00:02:47.009 line:80%
The accident happened
on the first snowfall.

00:02:48.177 --> 00:02:51.138 line:80%
So it became an unlucky day for me.

00:02:52.431 --> 00:02:53.682 line:80%
Mmm.

00:02:53.766 --> 00:02:55.601 line:80%
I know it's a lame jinx, though.

00:02:59.438 --> 00:03:00.481 line:80%
[sniffles]

00:03:00.564 --> 00:03:01.607 line:80%
[Chan groans]

00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:05.736 line:80%
Then I'll start hating
the first snow, too.

00:03:08.572 --> 00:03:09.740 line:80%
Oh, um…

00:03:09.823 --> 00:03:12.368 line:80%
I have a habit of copying other people.

00:03:17.414 --> 00:03:19.750 line:80%
I'm not sure if it's okay to ask this,

00:03:21.293 --> 00:03:25.547 line:80%
but when I talked about my mom's voice…

00:03:26.757 --> 00:03:29.218 line:80%
you said there's someone you miss.

00:03:30.094 --> 00:03:31.387 line:80%
That was your mother, right?

00:03:34.139 --> 00:03:35.849 line:80%
Your grandmother told me.

00:03:37.559 --> 00:03:41.021 line:80%
I was surprised when you spoke
like you experienced the same thing.

00:03:45.067 --> 00:03:47.569 line:80%
Uh…

00:03:48.654 --> 00:03:49.655 line:80%
Croissant.

00:03:49.738 --> 00:03:51.198 line:80%
Croissant?

00:03:52.741 --> 00:03:53.951 line:80%
The pastry?

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:56.537 line:80%
The crescent moon.

00:03:58.205 --> 00:03:59.748 line:80%
It's "croissant" in French.

00:04:00.416 --> 00:04:04.336 line:80%
Don't you crave croissants
when you see the crescent moon?

00:04:05.462 --> 00:04:06.463 line:80%
[stutters]

00:04:07.506 --> 00:04:09.341 line:80%
Anyway, your grandmother said--

00:04:09.425 --> 00:04:10.759 line:80%
What about the half-moon?

00:04:11.844 --> 00:04:13.554 line:80%
Omurice!

00:04:13.637 --> 00:04:14.638 line:80%
And the full moon?

00:04:14.722 --> 00:04:16.974 line:80%
It's pizza. Huh?

00:04:18.183 --> 00:04:20.394 line:80%
Was it just me, then? [chuckles]

00:04:21.854 --> 00:04:23.522 line:80%
I'm craving pizza.

00:04:24.773 --> 00:04:26.775 line:80%
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

00:04:34.533 --> 00:04:36.910 line:80%
Ben, we're here.

00:04:38.287 --> 00:04:40.497 line:80%
[inhales sharply] Are they not here yet?

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:44.793 line:80%
[Ben and team in English] Surprise!

00:04:44.877 --> 00:04:46.962 line:80%
[cheering, exclaiming]

00:04:48.339 --> 00:04:50.132 line:80%
-How have you been?
-I'm good, I'm good.

00:04:50.215 --> 00:04:52.551 line:80%
-It's great to see you here in Korea.
-Me too.

00:04:52.634 --> 00:04:54.303 line:80%
Let me quickly introduce her.

00:04:54.386 --> 00:04:56.764 line:80%
Guys, this is designer Haran Song.

00:04:57.348 --> 00:05:00.225 line:80%
[in Korean] Uh… Nice to meet you.

00:05:00.309 --> 00:05:03.854 line:80%
[hesitates] I'm Peter. Uh…

00:05:03.937 --> 00:05:06.231 line:80%
-[in English] It's so great to meet you.
-Hi, nice to meet you.

00:05:06.315 --> 00:05:08.067 line:80%
-This is my team.
-Nice to meet you. Hi.

00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:09.151 line:80%
Nice to meet you.

00:05:09.234 --> 00:05:11.695 line:80%
We're going to spend the morning
taking in the scenery,

00:05:11.779 --> 00:05:13.489 line:80%
visiting some historic sites,

00:05:13.572 --> 00:05:16.241 line:80%
and then we will head over
to Yangdong Village.

00:05:16.325 --> 00:05:21.246 line:80%
So on page 3, there's more information
about Yangdong Village.

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:26.168 line:80%
So as you can see, there's a big tree.
This tree is more than 500 years old.

00:05:26.251 --> 00:05:28.504 line:80%
It's really famous.

00:05:28.587 --> 00:05:31.382 line:80%
[Chan's grandma in Korean]
<i>So his father sent him to America,</i>

00:05:31.465 --> 00:05:34.468 line:80%
<i>and he suffered there.</i>

00:05:35.052 --> 00:05:36.553 line:80%
[Haran] <i>"Something terrible"?</i>

00:05:36.637 --> 00:05:38.973 line:80%
<i>-What happened in the US?</i>
-[♪ soft emotional music playing]

00:05:39.556 --> 00:05:42.267 line:80%
<i>Why won't he tell me about himself?</i>

00:05:42.351 --> 00:05:43.894 line:80%
[Peter in English] That's a great idea.
Let's use that tree.

00:05:43.978 --> 00:05:45.187 line:80%
It's famous in Yangdong.

00:05:45.270 --> 00:05:48.399 line:80%
[Ben in Korean] Ms. Song,
about the materials you sent over…

00:05:48.482 --> 00:05:49.525 line:80%
[Haran] Yes.

00:05:49.608 --> 00:05:52.069 line:80%
It's pretty decorative, right?

00:05:52.152 --> 00:05:53.445 line:80%
We'll turn it into a pattern.

00:05:53.529 --> 00:05:56.991 line:80%
Why am I someone you shouldn't like?

00:05:57.074 --> 00:05:59.076 line:80%
[♪ music continuing]

00:05:59.868 --> 00:06:01.870 line:80%
[indistinct chatter]

00:06:08.335 --> 00:06:10.379 line:80%
[wind whooshing]

00:06:10.462 --> 00:06:12.172 line:80%
-[leaves rustling]
-[birds chirping]

00:06:12.256 --> 00:06:13.257 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:06:13.340 --> 00:06:15.259 line:80%
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

00:06:15.342 --> 00:06:17.177 line:80%
[lively chatter]

00:06:17.261 --> 00:06:18.887 line:80%
-[group cheering]
-[Chan] Oh?

00:06:20.806 --> 00:06:22.808 line:80%
-[sighs]
-What are you doing?

00:06:22.891 --> 00:06:24.852 line:80%
Oh. Playing a game to pick the driver.

00:06:24.935 --> 00:06:26.645 line:80%
You saw our team, right?

00:06:26.729 --> 00:06:28.105 line:80%
They're all mischievous.

00:06:28.188 --> 00:06:29.189 line:80%
[laughter]

00:06:29.273 --> 00:06:30.649 line:80%
Did you lose?

00:06:30.733 --> 00:06:32.818 line:80%
-Then I'll drive--
-I'm the king of games.

00:06:33.569 --> 00:06:35.612 line:80%
I won, of course. [chuckles softly]

00:06:36.488 --> 00:06:37.656 line:80%
We're here!

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:38.949 line:80%
Hey, Sol!

00:06:39.033 --> 00:06:40.409 line:80%
Why are you alone?

00:06:40.492 --> 00:06:42.411 line:80%
Raemee is here!

00:06:42.494 --> 00:06:45.748 line:80%
Gosh, I just realized on the way here
how beautiful Gyeongju is.

00:06:45.831 --> 00:06:46.999 line:80%
It's totally my style.

00:06:47.082 --> 00:06:50.836 line:80%
It seems like
you're moving here. [chuckles]

00:06:50.919 --> 00:06:54.381 line:80%
I need this much luggage
at least to dress for the occasion.

00:06:54.465 --> 00:06:56.967 line:80%
-Don't play dumb!
-[chuckles]

00:06:57.051 --> 00:06:59.470 line:80%
-We're here, too.
-Me too.

00:07:00.387 --> 00:07:03.515 line:80%
[in English] Okay, everybody's here.
We'll leave in 10 minutes. Okay, guys?

00:07:03.599 --> 00:07:05.601 line:80%
[♪ uplifting song playing]

00:07:09.938 --> 00:07:11.607 line:80%
[lively chatter, laughter]

00:07:13.484 --> 00:07:14.777 line:80%
[in Korean] Let's lie down!

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:16.195 line:80%
[all sigh contentedly]

00:07:17.863 --> 00:07:19.531 line:80%
[Sol] This is so nice.

00:07:40.219 --> 00:07:41.637 line:20%
HWANGNIDAN STREET
GYEONGJU BREAD

00:07:41.720 --> 00:07:43.722 line:80%
[♪ song continues]

00:08:21.343 --> 00:08:22.886 line:80%
[Sol exclaims in awe]

00:08:22.970 --> 00:08:24.471 line:80%
[employees talking indistinctly]

00:08:29.143 --> 00:08:31.145 line:80%
[indistinct conversation continues]

00:08:37.234 --> 00:08:38.235 line:80%
-[inhales sharply]
-[Sol exclaims]

00:08:38.319 --> 00:08:39.653 line:80%
[mumbles]

00:08:40.404 --> 00:08:41.405 line:80%
Yes, Ms. Kim.

00:08:41.864 --> 00:08:42.865 line:80%
Seeing it in person,

00:08:42.948 --> 00:08:45.743 line:80%
I think we should emphasize
the Korean elements a bit more.

00:08:47.161 --> 00:08:50.622 line:80%
Then I'll come up with another sketch
with that in mind.

00:08:51.332 --> 00:08:52.541 line:80%
All right.

00:08:53.459 --> 00:08:54.460 line:80%
[line disconnects]

00:08:55.419 --> 00:08:58.130 line:80%
[sighs heavily] This is pretty tough.

00:09:01.550 --> 00:09:04.470 line:80%
Aren't you tired?
It's a tough schedule, isn't it?

00:09:04.553 --> 00:09:06.055 line:80%
It's okay. [chuckles]

00:09:07.389 --> 00:09:09.099 line:80%
Everyone seems excited, though.

00:09:09.183 --> 00:09:11.727 line:80%
You seem like friends
rather than colleagues.

00:09:11.810 --> 00:09:15.731 line:80%
We weren't this close,
but after Too Much joined us… [exclaims]

00:09:15.814 --> 00:09:17.149 line:80%
[both laugh]

00:09:17.232 --> 00:09:18.734 line:80%
You didn't join at the same time?

00:09:18.817 --> 00:09:21.987 line:80%
Too Much is several years my junior.
At school and at work.

00:09:22.071 --> 00:09:23.656 line:80%
He joined this field pretty late.

00:09:24.615 --> 00:09:28.035 line:80%
Oh. Then he studied something else
before animation?

00:09:28.118 --> 00:09:30.204 line:80%
[sighs] I don't know, either.

00:09:30.287 --> 00:09:35.084 line:80%
He never tells me
what he did before entering CalArts.

00:09:36.001 --> 00:09:37.920 line:80%
[in English] It's like he erased it.

00:09:39.296 --> 00:09:41.507 line:80%
[in Korean] Erasing his time…

00:09:43.926 --> 00:09:45.260 line:80%
Are you two badmouthing me?

00:09:45.344 --> 00:09:47.012 line:80%
[laughing] You caught us!

00:09:47.096 --> 00:09:48.597 line:80%
I'm fleeing!

00:09:49.598 --> 00:09:51.016 line:80%
You badmouthed me, didn't you?

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:52.935 line:80%
-No, we didn't.
-I think you did.

00:09:54.103 --> 00:09:55.604 line:80%
Did you sketch something?

00:09:55.688 --> 00:09:57.815 line:80%
-Oh… Yes. Do you want to see?
-Sure.

00:10:01.276 --> 00:10:02.277 line:80%
[Haran exclaims]

00:10:03.612 --> 00:10:04.613 line:80%
Wow.

00:10:04.697 --> 00:10:07.241 line:80%
Your grandmother said
you didn't draw for a while.

00:10:07.908 --> 00:10:10.202 line:80%
How did you end up drawing again?

00:10:10.285 --> 00:10:11.453 line:80%
I'm curious.

00:10:11.537 --> 00:10:13.038 line:80%
Was there a special reason?

00:10:13.914 --> 00:10:15.666 line:80%
Oh. Hmm…

00:10:17.167 --> 00:10:19.920 line:80%
[♪ sentimental music playing]

00:10:20.004 --> 00:10:21.005 line:20%
I'd like a ticket

00:10:21.672 --> 00:10:24.633 line:80%
for the earliest departure anywhere
except the US.

00:10:24.717 --> 00:10:26.677 line:80%
[in English] Hi, where are you from?

00:10:27.594 --> 00:10:30.597 line:80%
Well, anyway… Enjoy Florence.

00:10:41.275 --> 00:10:44.111 line:80%
THINGS TO GET RID OF: THE PAST
THINGS TO DO FROM NOW ON

00:10:46.947 --> 00:10:49.575 line:80%
THINGS I WANT TO DO FROM NOW ON

00:10:51.618 --> 00:10:54.538 line:80%
DRAW

00:10:56.081 --> 00:10:57.458 line:80%
[Chan in Korean] <i>I just…</i>

00:10:57.541 --> 00:10:58.542 line:80%
[sighs]

00:10:59.543 --> 00:11:01.295 line:80%
didn't want to live like a corpse.

00:11:02.546 --> 00:11:03.547 line:80%
A corpse?

00:11:04.757 --> 00:11:07.676 line:80%
Doesn't it feel like we time-traveled?

00:11:08.177 --> 00:11:11.096 line:80%
This tree is over 500 years old.

00:11:11.180 --> 00:11:12.181 line:80%
Mmm.

00:11:13.557 --> 00:11:15.559 line:80%
[♪ music continues]

00:11:24.443 --> 00:11:27.821 line:80%
If you can time travel,
when do you want to return to?

00:11:27.905 --> 00:11:29.740 line:80%
Mmm… I don't want to go back.

00:11:29.823 --> 00:11:30.949 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:11:31.033 --> 00:11:34.953 line:80%
I don't have a past I want to return to.

00:11:36.413 --> 00:11:38.749 line:80%
Doesn't everyone have
a certain moment, though?

00:11:40.376 --> 00:11:41.960 line:80%
You never know when you'll die.

00:11:42.753 --> 00:11:46.215 line:80%
You should enjoy your life
instead of regretting the past,

00:11:46.298 --> 00:11:47.675 line:80%
so you won't feel upset later.

00:11:49.301 --> 00:11:50.636 line:80%
[♪ pleasant music playing]

00:11:50.719 --> 00:11:51.929 line:80%
Mmm.

00:11:52.012 --> 00:11:54.139 line:80%
Maybe it's that free trial.

00:11:54.223 --> 00:11:56.058 line:80%
I do feel kind of excited these days.

00:11:56.767 --> 00:11:59.895 line:80%
We went to the Hangang River,
made pottery,

00:12:00.854 --> 00:12:01.981 line:80%
and came here.

00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:06.318 line:80%
You're doing great.

00:12:06.402 --> 00:12:10.531 line:80%
Keep enjoying your life
like this every day,

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:12.491 line:80%
even when…

00:12:13.409 --> 00:12:14.618 line:80%
I'm not here later.

00:12:36.557 --> 00:12:38.767 line:80%
-[♪ music fades]
-[elevator dings]

00:12:41.270 --> 00:12:43.731 line:80%
Oh? You changed your outfit.

00:12:43.814 --> 00:12:46.650 line:80%
You weren't wearing that earlier.
Why did you change?

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:51.196 line:80%
Oh… I just bought it
while doing some trend research.

00:12:51.280 --> 00:12:54.867 line:80%
That's strange.
It really isn't your style.

00:12:54.950 --> 00:12:57.036 line:80%
It looks like
you picked it out in a hurry.

00:12:57.119 --> 00:12:58.954 line:80%
Did I miss some kind of new trend?

00:12:59.038 --> 00:13:00.372 line:80%
-Or--
-Shut up.

00:13:00.456 --> 00:13:02.291 line:80%
You're so talkative.

00:13:02.374 --> 00:13:03.459 line:80%
[groans cutely]

00:13:03.542 --> 00:13:05.878 line:80%
I'm just curious about you.

00:13:05.961 --> 00:13:08.297 line:80%
This is my way
of expressing love and affection.

00:13:13.052 --> 00:13:14.553 line:80%
[♪ amusing music playing]

00:13:14.636 --> 00:13:17.056 line:80%
[Hayeong] <i>I'll just go meet Cha Min.</i>

00:13:26.148 --> 00:13:27.816 line:80%
<i>What's this awkward silence?</i>

00:13:27.900 --> 00:13:30.235 line:80%
<i>Say something, Hayeong.</i>

00:13:30.319 --> 00:13:33.364 line:80%
<i>You're usually talkative.</i>
<i>It'll seem like he's making you nervous.</i>

00:13:33.447 --> 00:13:36.700 line:80%
<i>Just tease him or something,</i>
<i>like you usually do.</i>

00:13:37.242 --> 00:13:38.243 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:13:38.327 --> 00:13:40.746 line:80%
-Is there something wrong?
-What?

00:13:40.829 --> 00:13:42.998 line:80%
You seem quieter than usual.

00:13:43.082 --> 00:13:44.375 line:80%
Do you think

00:13:44.458 --> 00:13:48.879 line:80%
I'm always…
[stuttering] just chatting loudly?

00:13:48.962 --> 00:13:50.381 line:80%
That's not what I meant.

00:13:51.256 --> 00:13:52.257 line:80%
Sorry.

00:13:53.550 --> 00:13:55.886 line:80%
But aren't you getting off?

00:13:55.969 --> 00:13:57.680 line:80%
Right. I am.

00:13:57.763 --> 00:14:00.224 line:80%
-[thuds]
-[♪ heart-fluttering music playing]

00:14:00.307 --> 00:14:01.558 line:80%
Be careful.

00:14:04.353 --> 00:14:05.354 line:80%
[clears throat]

00:14:08.482 --> 00:14:09.483 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:14:09.942 --> 00:14:10.943 line:80%
[grunts]

00:14:13.570 --> 00:14:14.571 line:80%
[sighs heavily]

00:14:23.580 --> 00:14:25.582 line:80%
[♪ melancholy music playing]

00:14:29.670 --> 00:14:31.922 line:80%
[cell phone vibrating]

00:14:37.136 --> 00:14:38.178 line:80%
Hey, Manjae.

00:14:38.262 --> 00:14:40.139 line:80%
Did you move or something?

00:14:40.222 --> 00:14:43.517 line:80%
You said you'd drop by sometime,
but you never came.

00:14:43.600 --> 00:14:46.854 line:80%
Sorry, I've been pretty busy.

00:14:46.937 --> 00:14:49.315 line:80%
Why don't I drop by after work today?

00:14:49.398 --> 00:14:51.275 line:80%
Sure. Come and see Genius, too.

00:14:53.235 --> 00:14:54.236 line:80%
[Manjae chuckles]

00:14:54.737 --> 00:14:56.113 line:80%
Okay. I'll see you later.

00:15:10.294 --> 00:15:11.670 line:80%
[sighs]

00:15:11.754 --> 00:15:12.755 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:15:15.758 --> 00:15:16.759 line:80%
[brakes hiss]

00:15:19.803 --> 00:15:21.639 line:80%
Hey, it's Yougyum.

00:15:22.139 --> 00:15:23.182 line:80%
What?

00:15:23.682 --> 00:15:25.684 line:80%
He just came out of a jewelry shop.

00:15:25.768 --> 00:15:28.020 line:80%
I bet he bought matching rings.

00:15:28.687 --> 00:15:29.772 line:80%
You're so lucky, Hadam.

00:15:35.861 --> 00:15:37.446 line:80%
Matching rings?

00:15:37.529 --> 00:15:39.239 line:80%
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

00:15:40.491 --> 00:15:41.492 line:80%
[chuckles softly]

00:15:42.660 --> 00:15:45.371 line:80%
[employees] Thank you for the food!

00:15:45.454 --> 00:15:47.706 line:80%
[indistinct chatter]

00:15:52.586 --> 00:15:54.254 line:80%
[in English] Try this one, try this one.

00:15:57.925 --> 00:16:00.302 line:80%
[Raemee in Korean] Yummy. This is amazing.

00:16:02.388 --> 00:16:03.472 line:80%
I'll eat those for you.

00:16:03.555 --> 00:16:05.891 line:80%
The snot and neon aliens.

00:16:06.684 --> 00:16:07.685 line:80%
Thanks. [chuckles]

00:16:08.936 --> 00:16:11.981 line:80%
[in English] Don't you guys think that
Yangdong Village was just so gorgeous?

00:16:12.064 --> 00:16:14.274 line:80%
It was really unique, don't you think?

00:16:14.358 --> 00:16:16.777 line:80%
I totally agree.
It kind of felt like it was timeless.

00:16:16.860 --> 00:16:19.947 line:80%
Actually, I think it feels
even better than the photo. Right?

00:16:20.030 --> 00:16:21.782 line:80%
[female guest] Yeah, it's so beautiful.

00:16:21.865 --> 00:16:25.202 line:80%
But do you know the scene
where Won first goes back to the past?

00:16:27.037 --> 00:16:32.209 line:80%
Uh… Maybe we can make that moment
a little bit deeper. Do you guys agree?

00:16:32.292 --> 00:16:35.045 line:80%
[Ben] Maybe that's exactly
what we should do, yeah.

00:16:35.129 --> 00:16:36.130 line:80%
[male guest] Awesome.

00:16:36.213 --> 00:16:38.090 line:80%
-Okay, then… Mmm.
-[Ben] Let's do it.

00:16:38.173 --> 00:16:40.300 line:80%
-Thank you so much. Let's just eat first.
-[laughter]

00:16:40.384 --> 00:16:42.177 line:80%
[in Korean] All together. One, two, three!

00:16:42.261 --> 00:16:45.014 line:80%
[all] The ocean!

00:16:45.097 --> 00:16:47.099 line:80%
[♪ upbeat music playing]

00:16:49.184 --> 00:16:51.186 line:80%
[yelling, exclaiming]

00:16:52.730 --> 00:16:54.148 line:80%
[laughter]

00:16:54.898 --> 00:16:57.026 line:80%
Wait!

00:16:57.109 --> 00:16:58.986 line:80%
No, wait! Hey, Raemee!

00:17:05.075 --> 00:17:07.077 line:80%
[indistinct chatter]

00:17:14.001 --> 00:17:16.003 line:80%
-[hums in thought, speaks indistinctly]
-[inhales sharply]

00:17:18.505 --> 00:17:20.507 line:80%
[waves crashing]

00:17:21.133 --> 00:17:22.134 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:17:36.690 --> 00:17:37.691 line:80%
[Haran sighs wearily]

00:17:37.775 --> 00:17:39.902 line:80%
I can't even decide on a concept.

00:17:41.528 --> 00:17:43.322 line:80%
You there, who's mulling over pens.

00:17:44.198 --> 00:17:47.284 line:80%
Do you want to go see the sea cave
to clear your head?

00:17:47.368 --> 00:17:48.410 line:80%
[chuckles softly]

00:17:48.494 --> 00:17:49.953 line:80%
[in English] Nice timing.

00:17:50.037 --> 00:17:51.955 line:80%
[in Korean] I needed
a reason to take a break.

00:17:52.039 --> 00:17:53.374 line:80%
[chuckles]

00:17:56.585 --> 00:17:57.628 line:80%
Oh, right.

00:17:59.922 --> 00:18:01.674 line:80%
I never told you that, though.

00:18:03.217 --> 00:18:05.010 line:80%
I told you I don't eat oysters,

00:18:05.094 --> 00:18:08.097 line:80%
but I never told you
eggplants seemed like neon aliens.

00:18:09.556 --> 00:18:10.641 line:80%
[Chan] <i>I'll eat those for you.</i>

00:18:10.724 --> 00:18:12.685 line:80%
The snot and neon aliens.

00:18:12.768 --> 00:18:14.520 line:80%
[Haran] <i>It's neon-colored. Yuck!</i>

00:18:14.603 --> 00:18:16.855 line:80%
<i>The taste of a neon alien. </i>[retches]

00:18:16.939 --> 00:18:18.941 line:80%
[♪ mysterious music playing]

00:18:19.650 --> 00:18:20.651 line:80%
Uh…

00:18:24.822 --> 00:18:27.074 line:80%
No, how else would you know?

00:18:27.157 --> 00:18:28.200 line:80%
I guess I told you.

00:18:28.909 --> 00:18:30.411 line:80%
Sorry, I must've forgotten.

00:18:30.494 --> 00:18:31.495 line:80%
Is it this way?

00:18:31.578 --> 00:18:32.788 line:80%
-[♪ music fades]
-[Haran chuckles]

00:18:43.590 --> 00:18:45.592 line:80%
[waves crashing]

00:18:47.344 --> 00:18:48.345 line:80%
What are you doing?

00:18:53.559 --> 00:18:56.603 line:80%
Don't you want to ride a plane
when you see a vapor trail?

00:18:58.439 --> 00:19:00.441 line:80%
I actually rode one after seeing one.

00:19:01.734 --> 00:19:05.070 line:80%
I went to meet the person
who gave me that fountain pen I lost.

00:19:06.905 --> 00:19:08.866 line:80%
I used to work at a different company,

00:19:09.491 --> 00:19:14.038 line:80%
and he was the brother of my team leader
who really cared for me.

00:19:15.039 --> 00:19:18.625 line:80%
But soon after we started dating,
he went to Boston to study.

00:19:18.709 --> 00:19:20.627 line:80%
[♪ dramatic music playing]

00:19:21.879 --> 00:19:23.047 line:80%
[Hyeokchan] <i>Nice to meet you.</i>

00:19:23.130 --> 00:19:25.257 line:80%
<i>I'm Kang Hyeokchan.</i>

00:19:25.341 --> 00:19:26.675 line:80%
I'm glad you're Korean, too.

00:19:26.759 --> 00:19:27.926 line:80%
I hope we get along.

00:19:30.095 --> 00:19:31.138 line:80%
[breathing heavily]

00:19:31.847 --> 00:19:33.057 line:80%
Are you okay?

00:19:33.724 --> 00:19:35.726 line:80%
[metallic clink echoing]

00:19:38.520 --> 00:19:40.856 line:80%
Are you all right? You've gone pale.

00:19:41.982 --> 00:19:43.317 line:80%
[inhales sharply]

00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:45.653 line:80%
-If I'm not okay, will you carry me?
-[♪ music fades]

00:19:46.362 --> 00:19:48.280 line:80%
Are you seriously joking right now?

00:19:48.364 --> 00:19:49.948 line:80%
Are you sure you're okay?

00:19:51.325 --> 00:19:53.118 line:80%
I'll be okay.

00:19:54.370 --> 00:19:56.080 line:80%
It's all going to be okay.

00:19:56.163 --> 00:19:57.748 line:80%
[♪ solemn music playing]

00:20:05.381 --> 00:20:06.382 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:20:06.465 --> 00:20:08.717 line:80%
-Yougyum!
-Hey, Hadam.

00:20:11.178 --> 00:20:14.473 line:80%
My academy ends at 9:00 p.m.
Should we meet after?

00:20:14.556 --> 00:20:15.849 line:80%
What?

00:20:15.933 --> 00:20:17.851 line:80%
Did we plan to meet today?

00:20:18.435 --> 00:20:19.603 line:80%
Mmm…

00:20:19.687 --> 00:20:23.857 line:80%
No, but I think you have a reason
to meet me later.

00:20:23.941 --> 00:20:25.067 line:80%
I don't.

00:20:25.734 --> 00:20:28.654 line:80%
Why don't you spend some time
with your grandma--

00:20:28.737 --> 00:20:31.323 line:80%
Why are you suddenly
bringing up my grandma?

00:20:31.407 --> 00:20:32.533 line:80%
What?

00:20:32.616 --> 00:20:33.951 line:80%
[♪ whimsical music playing]

00:20:34.034 --> 00:20:36.120 line:80%
Oh… Well…

00:20:36.203 --> 00:20:37.663 line:80%
Hey, Changmo!

00:20:37.746 --> 00:20:40.833 line:80%
I have something urgent
to discuss with Changmo, so I have to go.

00:20:40.916 --> 00:20:42.376 line:80%
Hey, Changmo!

00:20:44.211 --> 00:20:47.715 line:80%
What? Changmo isn't even there.
[hums excitedly]

00:20:48.590 --> 00:20:51.093 line:80%
[scoffs] He should hurry up
and give me the ring.

00:20:52.469 --> 00:20:56.140 line:80%
Unfortunately, it seems like
he gave the ring to Han Sora.

00:20:56.223 --> 00:20:57.224 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:20:57.308 --> 00:20:59.351 line:80%
She didn't have that a few days ago.

00:20:59.435 --> 00:21:00.936 line:80%
But she was wearing this
in her recent feed.

00:21:02.104 --> 00:21:04.064 line:80%
[scoffs] Don't be ridiculous.

00:21:04.857 --> 00:21:07.609 line:80%
If a girl group trainee with her looks
hits on him,

00:21:07.693 --> 00:21:09.528 line:80%
he could easily fall for her.

00:21:14.325 --> 00:21:16.327 line:80%
[♪ whimsical music playing]

00:21:19.288 --> 00:21:21.373 line:80%
[sighs] That's nonsense.

00:21:23.208 --> 00:21:24.209 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:21:24.293 --> 00:21:25.294 line:80%
GUARDIAN

00:21:25.377 --> 00:21:27.171 line:80%
[♪ jazz music playing over speakers]

00:21:28.047 --> 00:21:29.214 line:80%
[Manjae chuckles]

00:21:30.215 --> 00:21:32.009 line:80%
I wanted to give you this.

00:21:32.092 --> 00:21:36.347 line:80%
It finally found its owner
after over 50 years.

00:21:36.430 --> 00:21:37.514 line:80%
[chuckles]

00:21:40.851 --> 00:21:43.062 line:80%
What? "La Vie en rose"?

00:21:43.979 --> 00:21:46.357 line:80%
-This is my favorite song.
-[chuckles]

00:21:46.440 --> 00:21:48.984 line:80%
But what did you mean
by this finding its owner?

00:21:49.068 --> 00:21:52.696 line:80%
You were humming that song all the time
when we lived in Chuncheon.

00:21:52.780 --> 00:21:55.532 line:80%
-I played it with the harmonica, too.
-[gasps]

00:21:55.616 --> 00:21:56.700 line:80%
Right.

00:21:57.284 --> 00:21:58.285 line:80%
I remember.

00:21:58.369 --> 00:22:00.037 line:80%
After I went to college in Seoul

00:22:00.120 --> 00:22:03.457 line:80%
and heard you got accepted
to a medical school the next year,

00:22:03.540 --> 00:22:06.377 line:80%
I went to Chuncheon to give you this.

00:22:06.460 --> 00:22:09.129 line:80%
I waited by the tree
where we always hung out,

00:22:09.213 --> 00:22:12.049 line:80%
but you never showed.

00:22:12.132 --> 00:22:13.217 line:80%
You waited for me?

00:22:13.300 --> 00:22:17.471 line:80%
It snowed like crazy that day.

00:22:17.554 --> 00:22:20.391 line:80%
I almost became a snowman
waiting for you there.

00:22:20.474 --> 00:22:21.475 line:80%
[both laugh]

00:22:21.558 --> 00:22:25.229 line:80%
I only heard the news later on.

00:22:25.312 --> 00:22:28.524 line:80%
The news that I ran off with my tuition
and hopped on a flight to Paris?

00:22:28.607 --> 00:22:30.442 line:80%
Yes! [laughs]

00:22:30.526 --> 00:22:34.446 line:80%
I didn't get to give you this record,
so I just listened to it.

00:22:34.530 --> 00:22:36.991 line:80%
[gasps softly] It was so nice.

00:22:37.074 --> 00:22:40.119 line:80%
That's how I got obsessed
and started collecting vinyls.

00:22:40.995 --> 00:22:42.871 line:80%
And this is the result.

00:22:42.955 --> 00:22:46.625 line:80%
It's all your fault, Kim Nabong.

00:22:46.709 --> 00:22:48.210 line:80%
[laughs]

00:22:49.628 --> 00:22:50.879 line:80%
Is that so?

00:22:52.798 --> 00:22:53.799 line:80%
[sighs]

00:22:54.758 --> 00:22:58.012 line:80%
We were dazzling back then.

00:23:01.765 --> 00:23:03.017 line:80%
It's nice seeing you again.

00:23:04.184 --> 00:23:07.271 line:80%
I'd been so busy pushing forward
that I'd forgotten about our old hometown.

00:23:08.480 --> 00:23:09.815 line:80%
I agree.

00:23:09.898 --> 00:23:10.983 line:80%
[both laugh]

00:23:11.066 --> 00:23:13.110 line:80%
Instead of just reminiscing,

00:23:13.193 --> 00:23:15.821 line:80%
why don't we visit Chuncheon sometime?

00:23:15.904 --> 00:23:16.905 line:80%
Chuncheon?

00:23:16.989 --> 00:23:19.742 line:80%
Aren't you curious
whether that tree is still there

00:23:20.242 --> 00:23:23.037 line:80%
and how much our neighborhood has changed?

00:23:23.120 --> 00:23:24.371 line:80%
[gasps]

00:23:24.455 --> 00:23:25.789 line:80%
Right.

00:23:26.582 --> 00:23:28.292 line:80%
All right, let's go there sometime.

00:23:28.375 --> 00:23:30.085 line:80%
Okay. Let's do that.

00:23:30.502 --> 00:23:32.504 line:80%
[both laughing]

00:23:36.300 --> 00:23:38.302 line:80%
[indistinct chatter]

00:23:43.223 --> 00:23:44.558 line:80%
-[chatter continues]
-[sighs softly]

00:23:44.642 --> 00:23:45.976 line:80%
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

00:23:46.769 --> 00:23:49.688 line:80%
[Chan] <i>Lab, glass tube, blood…</i>

00:23:50.397 --> 00:23:51.482 line:80%
<i>Whose blood?</i>

00:23:52.149 --> 00:23:53.275 line:80%
[sighs]

00:23:53.942 --> 00:23:55.277 line:80%
Yes, Ms. Kim.

00:23:56.070 --> 00:23:58.280 line:80%
Je Raemee sent his design?

00:23:59.948 --> 00:24:02.076 line:80%
Oh. Sorry, I haven't
sketched anything yet.

00:24:04.161 --> 00:24:06.580 line:80%
[doctor] <i>If you don't want to suffer again</i>
<i>because of your past,</i>

00:24:06.664 --> 00:24:08.999 line:80%
<i>it would be best</i>
<i>to keep a distance from her.</i>

00:24:10.084 --> 00:24:11.585 line:80%
[Chan] <i>Did something else happen</i>

00:24:12.503 --> 00:24:14.213 line:80%
<i>besides the explosion?</i>

00:24:15.756 --> 00:24:17.841 line:80%
[groans] Hurry up. Why are you so slow?

00:24:17.925 --> 00:24:19.343 line:80%
-Sorry.
-[♪ music fades]

00:24:19.426 --> 00:24:22.012 line:80%
[in English] All right, everybody.
Let's head back and get some rest.

00:24:22.096 --> 00:24:23.305 line:80%
Yeah, let's go.

00:24:23.389 --> 00:24:25.391 line:80%
[Sol in Korean] We'll see you later.

00:24:25.474 --> 00:24:27.059 line:80%
[indistinct chatter]

00:24:27.768 --> 00:24:29.561 line:80%
Oh? Where's Ms. Song?

00:24:30.396 --> 00:24:33.482 line:80%
-Huh?
-What? Weren't you with her?

00:24:34.233 --> 00:24:35.901 line:80%
You were hanging out the whole time.

00:24:35.985 --> 00:24:39.113 line:80%
She said she forgot her scarf.
She went to get it.

00:24:39.196 --> 00:24:41.448 line:80%
Goodness. She's a klutz sometimes.

00:24:41.532 --> 00:24:43.409 line:80%
[leaves rustling]

00:24:47.287 --> 00:24:49.248 line:80%
[thunder rumbling]

00:24:49.331 --> 00:24:50.332 line:80%
Oh, uh…

00:24:50.791 --> 00:24:52.501 line:80%
I'll go and get her. You go ahead.

00:24:52.584 --> 00:24:54.044 line:80%
[♪ tense music playing]

00:25:00.342 --> 00:25:01.510 line:80%
Ms. Song!

00:25:02.553 --> 00:25:03.679 line:80%
Ms. Song!

00:25:04.430 --> 00:25:05.723 line:80%
[pants]

00:25:05.806 --> 00:25:07.433 line:80%
Song Haran! [sighs]

00:25:07.516 --> 00:25:08.684 line:80%
[Haran whimpers]

00:25:08.767 --> 00:25:10.352 line:80%
[pants]

00:25:10.436 --> 00:25:11.478 line:80%
-Oh?
-[♪ music ends]

00:25:11.562 --> 00:25:12.563 line:80%
Why were you--

00:25:12.646 --> 00:25:13.897 line:80%
[panting] Why are you so fast?

00:25:13.981 --> 00:25:16.191 line:80%
I… [pants]

00:25:16.775 --> 00:25:18.527 line:80%
I thought I'd left this here,

00:25:18.610 --> 00:25:20.571 line:80%
but I found it in my pocket
and headed down.

00:25:20.654 --> 00:25:22.323 line:80%
But then I heard you went to find me.

00:25:22.406 --> 00:25:24.950 line:80%
I kept calling, but you wouldn't answer.

00:25:25.034 --> 00:25:26.785 line:80%
[grunts] I'm sorry.

00:25:27.202 --> 00:25:28.871 line:80%
I guess I didn't hear it over the rain.

00:25:28.954 --> 00:25:30.873 line:80%
I should've been more careful.

00:25:30.956 --> 00:25:32.458 line:80%
You're always apologizing.

00:25:32.541 --> 00:25:34.084 line:80%
-Let's go.
-Okay.

00:25:34.168 --> 00:25:35.377 line:80%
[thunderclap]

00:25:35.461 --> 00:25:36.962 line:80%
[both exclaim nervously]

00:25:37.588 --> 00:25:39.089 line:80%
-[exclaims frantically]
-[grunts]

00:25:40.341 --> 00:25:42.051 line:80%
-[exclaims]
-Let's get out of the rain.

00:25:42.134 --> 00:25:43.761 line:80%
-Over there.
-[Haran exclaims, squeals]

00:25:48.891 --> 00:25:50.309 line:80%
Sit down.

00:25:51.101 --> 00:25:53.312 line:80%
Oh. Thanks. [sighs]

00:25:53.812 --> 00:25:54.813 line:80%
[groans]

00:25:54.897 --> 00:25:56.440 line:80%
Are you hurt?

00:25:56.523 --> 00:25:58.108 line:80%
No, it's nothing. [chuckles awkwardly]

00:25:58.192 --> 00:26:00.277 line:80%
-[rain pattering]
-[Chan sighs wearily]

00:26:00.778 --> 00:26:03.405 line:80%
You shouldn't climb
with your shoelaces so loose.

00:26:05.157 --> 00:26:06.533 line:80%
Your feet must have hurt a lot.

00:26:06.617 --> 00:26:08.369 line:80%
-Hey, it's dirty.
-[grunts]

00:26:09.370 --> 00:26:11.163 line:80%
Tell me if it keeps hurting.

00:26:11.789 --> 00:26:13.499 line:80%
I'll carry you if I have to.

00:26:16.418 --> 00:26:18.420 line:80%
[♪ melancholy music playing]

00:26:19.713 --> 00:26:21.590 line:80%
I can't hear on this side.

00:26:21.674 --> 00:26:22.675 line:80%
[gasps lightly]

00:26:22.758 --> 00:26:25.511 line:80%
[Chan's grandma]
<i>So his father sent him to America,</i>

00:26:25.594 --> 00:26:28.764 line:80%
and he suffered there.

00:26:30.224 --> 00:26:31.225 line:80%
[sighs]

00:26:32.101 --> 00:26:33.602 line:80%
To be honest, I'm curious.

00:26:34.353 --> 00:26:35.646 line:80%
About what?

00:26:36.230 --> 00:26:38.774 line:80%
About what I heard from your grandmother.

00:26:39.900 --> 00:26:42.820 line:80%
I want to know what happened in America,

00:26:44.196 --> 00:26:47.408 line:80%
what you meant by being trapped in winter,

00:26:47.491 --> 00:26:49.910 line:80%
and who freed you from it.

00:26:50.536 --> 00:26:53.455 line:80%
I'm getting more comfortable around you,

00:26:54.123 --> 00:26:56.667 line:80%
and I've been telling you
things about myself,

00:26:56.750 --> 00:26:58.085 line:80%
but…

00:26:58.919 --> 00:27:01.422 line:80%
you don't seem to be telling me
much about yourself.

00:27:07.511 --> 00:27:08.512 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:27:09.263 --> 00:27:11.682 line:80%
I started studying animation
six years ago.

00:27:12.391 --> 00:27:15.102 line:80%
I worked my butt off and graduated early

00:27:15.185 --> 00:27:18.147 line:80%
then entered my current company
as a character designer.

00:27:18.230 --> 00:27:20.649 line:80%
I became a supervisor by luck

00:27:20.733 --> 00:27:23.277 line:80%
since Won was a Korean character.

00:27:25.029 --> 00:27:28.240 line:80%
[grunts] I commute by bike

00:27:28.949 --> 00:27:31.869 line:80%
since the office
is a 10-minute ride from home.

00:27:31.952 --> 00:27:34.079 line:80%
You met my teammates, right?

00:27:34.163 --> 00:27:35.289 line:80%
Everyone's really close.

00:27:35.998 --> 00:27:37.166 line:80%
-And--
-Wait.

00:27:39.001 --> 00:27:41.170 line:80%
-What are you talking about?
-I'm sorry,

00:27:42.921 --> 00:27:44.590 line:80%
but I'll use it now.

00:27:46.967 --> 00:27:49.511 line:80%
You said it's okay
to keep some secrets to yourself.

00:27:49.595 --> 00:27:51.680 line:80%
You tell me a secret too next time.

00:27:51.764 --> 00:27:53.682 line:80%
We can keep big secrets to ourselves.

00:27:53.766 --> 00:27:55.684 line:80%
<i>Just a small one.</i>

00:27:55.768 --> 00:27:59.229 line:80%
I'll tell you everything
about the present…

00:27:59.855 --> 00:28:02.107 line:80%
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

00:28:02.191 --> 00:28:03.525 line:80%
but I'll use that card…

00:28:05.444 --> 00:28:06.695 line:80%
for my past.

00:28:08.197 --> 00:28:09.198 line:80%
Sorry.

00:28:11.659 --> 00:28:12.660 line:80%
Ah…

00:28:13.577 --> 00:28:14.578 line:80%
Oh, no.

00:28:14.662 --> 00:28:16.747 line:80%
I guess I was being really rude.

00:28:17.373 --> 00:28:20.417 line:80%
[stutters] Right, we agreed
to do a three-month trial,

00:28:20.501 --> 00:28:22.294 line:80%
but I was prying too much.

00:28:23.337 --> 00:28:26.048 line:80%
[stutters] I was being selfish.
I'm so sorry.

00:28:32.137 --> 00:28:33.138 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:28:35.891 --> 00:28:36.892 line:80%
[men chuckling]

00:28:36.976 --> 00:28:38.102 line:80%
[talking indistinctly]

00:28:38.185 --> 00:28:40.688 line:80%
This looks so delicious.

00:28:41.355 --> 00:28:42.481 line:80%
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

00:28:44.525 --> 00:28:46.568 line:80%
-[in English] Thank you.
-Yeah, no problem.

00:28:46.652 --> 00:28:49.947 line:80%
[in Korean] The staff prepared this since
the costume team is leaving tomorrow.

00:28:50.030 --> 00:28:52.241 line:80%
-Thank you.
-That's so nice.

00:28:52.324 --> 00:28:53.534 line:80%
I'm so touched.

00:28:53.617 --> 00:28:55.661 line:80%
Do we seriously have to leave this behind

00:28:55.744 --> 00:28:57.705 line:80%
-and return to Seoul?
-[sighs]

00:28:57.788 --> 00:28:59.999 line:80%
[sighs] I can't leave!

00:29:00.082 --> 00:29:02.793 line:80%
Since this is our last night,

00:29:02.876 --> 00:29:04.795 line:80%
let us all have a drink.

00:29:04.878 --> 00:29:07.297 line:80%
[indistinct chatter]

00:29:07.381 --> 00:29:08.841 line:80%
Everyone… [in English] Cheers!

00:29:08.924 --> 00:29:11.885 line:80%
[group] Cheers! [exclaiming]

00:29:11.969 --> 00:29:14.346 line:80%
[in Korean] ♪ <i>Altogether</i>
<i>Game start </i>♪

00:29:14.430 --> 00:29:15.723 line:80%
-Numbers game! One!
-Two!

00:29:15.806 --> 00:29:16.807 line:80%
Three!

00:29:16.890 --> 00:29:18.142 line:80%
-[Sol cheers]
-[guest laughs]

00:29:18.225 --> 00:29:20.436 line:80%
-[all in English] Drink!
-[exclaims]

00:29:20.519 --> 00:29:21.645 line:80%
[in Korean] <i>♪ Drink up </i>♪

00:29:21.729 --> 00:29:23.272 line:80%
It's my first time seeing her drink.

00:29:23.355 --> 00:29:25.357 line:80%
Wait, stop. I have to film this.

00:29:25.441 --> 00:29:27.234 line:80%
-[Sol] Can you drink like a beer model?
-[exclaims]

00:29:27.318 --> 00:29:28.986 line:80%
No…

00:29:29.069 --> 00:29:30.988 line:80%
-[Sol cheers, applauds]
-Why are you so pretty?

00:29:32.781 --> 00:29:33.782 line:80%
[sighs]

00:29:33.866 --> 00:29:36.076 line:80%
♪ <i>Altogether</i>
<i>Game start </i>♪

00:29:36.160 --> 00:29:37.286 line:80%
♪ <i>Three, six, nine </i>♪

00:29:37.369 --> 00:29:38.495 line:80%
[all] ♪ <i>Three, six, nine </i>♪

00:29:38.579 --> 00:29:41.498 line:80%
[game continues indistinctly]

00:29:45.085 --> 00:29:47.546 line:80%
Why are you suddenly so serious?
It doesn't suit you.

00:29:48.047 --> 00:29:49.673 line:80%
[inhales deeply] Ben.

00:29:50.174 --> 00:29:51.550 line:80%
Hiding something

00:29:52.384 --> 00:29:54.094 line:80%
and not telling the truth

00:29:55.429 --> 00:29:57.389 line:80%
is the same as lying, right?

00:29:57.973 --> 00:29:58.974 line:80%
That's so random.

00:30:00.142 --> 00:30:01.226 line:80%
Hide what, though?

00:30:01.310 --> 00:30:06.148 line:80%
You mean like how Aladdin
hid the fact that he was a petty thief?

00:30:06.231 --> 00:30:07.232 line:80%
[chuckles softly]

00:30:08.067 --> 00:30:09.652 line:80%
I guess it's similar.

00:30:11.195 --> 00:30:12.446 line:80%
It's just…

00:30:12.529 --> 00:30:15.366 line:80%
The other person is being honest with me,

00:30:17.034 --> 00:30:18.577 line:80%
but if I keep…

00:30:20.204 --> 00:30:21.455 line:80%
hiding things

00:30:22.289 --> 00:30:24.166 line:80%
and never being honest,

00:30:25.292 --> 00:30:27.086 line:80%
what will happen in the end?

00:30:29.630 --> 00:30:30.631 line:80%
Ah.

00:30:32.049 --> 00:30:33.092 line:80%
Do you remember?

00:30:33.801 --> 00:30:36.845 line:80%
[in English] What the genie says
to Aladdin when he says

00:30:37.930 --> 00:30:39.848 line:80%
he wants to keep pretending
to be a prince?

00:30:41.016 --> 00:30:42.017 line:80%
Mmm.

00:30:43.394 --> 00:30:47.564 line:80%
[in Korean] The more you gain
with deception,

00:30:49.900 --> 00:30:53.153 line:80%
the less you can truly gain.

00:30:53.570 --> 00:30:54.655 line:80%
That's right.

00:30:55.823 --> 00:30:58.242 line:80%
It may seem like
you're gaining something now,

00:30:58.325 --> 00:31:01.161 line:80%
but you'll probably end up
paying the price for it.

00:31:02.621 --> 00:31:03.831 line:80%
Paying the price…

00:31:03.914 --> 00:31:05.958 line:80%
[waves crashing]

00:31:07.543 --> 00:31:09.962 line:80%
[indistinct chatter]

00:31:26.312 --> 00:31:27.771 line:80%
What are you doing here alone?

00:31:28.689 --> 00:31:29.690 line:80%
[chuckles softly]

00:31:30.316 --> 00:31:32.276 line:80%
I'm trying to sober up
so I can drink more.

00:31:32.943 --> 00:31:34.653 line:80%
It's been a while since I drank.

00:31:35.362 --> 00:31:36.780 line:80%
You're a heavy drinker.

00:31:37.406 --> 00:31:38.824 line:80%
How's your foot?

00:31:39.408 --> 00:31:41.660 line:80%
You hurt yourself
because of Grandma's scarf.

00:31:42.578 --> 00:31:43.620 line:80%
I'm okay.

00:31:44.288 --> 00:31:45.289 line:80%
[Haran grunts]

00:31:47.833 --> 00:31:48.834 line:80%
[Chan grunts]

00:31:49.960 --> 00:31:50.961 line:80%
Look, aren't they pretty?

00:31:53.297 --> 00:31:55.132 line:80%
-[chuckles]
-[sighs]

00:31:55.632 --> 00:31:58.927 line:80%
Maybe it's because I lost
the pen I used for seven years,

00:31:59.011 --> 00:32:01.555 line:80%
but I couldn't sketch anything
during the two days here.

00:32:02.765 --> 00:32:05.309 line:80%
Maybe it's because
I couldn't stop thinking about it.

00:32:05.392 --> 00:32:07.227 line:80%
I've been so distracted lately.

00:32:08.646 --> 00:32:13.859 line:80%
Until now, I thought that pen was special
because of the person who gifted it to me.

00:32:15.402 --> 00:32:17.237 line:80%
But I'm not so sure now.

00:32:17.780 --> 00:32:20.366 line:80%
Maybe I just feel strange

00:32:20.449 --> 00:32:23.369 line:80%
because I lost something
my hand had gotten used to

00:32:23.452 --> 00:32:25.829 line:80%
after all those years.

00:32:28.499 --> 00:32:31.418 line:80%
The person who gave me that pen died.

00:32:33.170 --> 00:32:35.756 line:80%
I guess that's why
I was so attached to it.

00:32:36.799 --> 00:32:38.634 line:80%
Not long ago,

00:32:38.717 --> 00:32:42.721 line:80%
I would have done anything I could
to avoid coming here.

00:32:42.805 --> 00:32:44.306 line:80%
But this time,

00:32:44.807 --> 00:32:47.810 line:80%
I had quite a lot of fun.

00:32:48.352 --> 00:32:49.728 line:80%
Like I was on a spring picnic.

00:32:49.812 --> 00:32:51.605 line:80%
[♪ pleasant music playing]

00:32:51.689 --> 00:32:53.565 line:80%
I guess we have grown quite close,

00:32:54.233 --> 00:32:57.528 line:80%
seeing how I'm telling you
things I'm not okay with.

00:32:58.696 --> 00:33:02.616 line:80%
You know we're not real friends
if we're always pretending to be okay.

00:33:07.329 --> 00:33:09.999 line:80%
Thank you for asking to be friends

00:33:11.458 --> 00:33:12.960 line:80%
and for knocking on my door.

00:33:13.919 --> 00:33:15.421 line:80%
You made me stop hiding,

00:33:16.463 --> 00:33:20.676 line:80%
and you made me
able to tell you sad things, too.

00:33:22.803 --> 00:33:25.431 line:80%
Stop thanking me. I didn't do anything.

00:33:25.514 --> 00:33:26.932 line:80%
Thank you.

00:33:27.016 --> 00:33:29.685 line:80%
I just feel like
pouring my heart out today.

00:33:31.270 --> 00:33:32.980 line:80%
I really am grateful.

00:33:41.280 --> 00:33:44.033 line:80%
[sighs] Can I borrow that for a moment?

00:33:45.367 --> 00:33:46.660 line:80%
-This?
-Yes.

00:33:55.085 --> 00:33:56.086 line:80%
Odd or even?

00:33:56.545 --> 00:33:58.047 line:80%
That's so random.

00:33:58.130 --> 00:34:00.215 line:80%
Is there a prize if I guess right?

00:34:01.925 --> 00:34:02.926 line:80%
If you guess right,

00:34:04.970 --> 00:34:06.972 line:80%
I'll tell you everything.

00:34:07.931 --> 00:34:09.099 line:80%
I feel like

00:34:10.559 --> 00:34:12.519 line:80%
telling you everything today, too.

00:34:13.729 --> 00:34:16.065 line:80%
-Tell me what?
-I think I should stop

00:34:16.148 --> 00:34:17.399 line:80%
hiding things about myself.

00:34:18.692 --> 00:34:19.777 line:80%
Oh…

00:34:19.860 --> 00:34:22.529 line:80%
If it's because of what I said,
you don't have to--

00:34:22.613 --> 00:34:23.781 line:80%
Odd or even?

00:34:23.864 --> 00:34:25.324 line:80%
[♪ pleasant music continuing]

00:34:38.170 --> 00:34:39.171 line:80%
Odd.

00:34:50.474 --> 00:34:51.600 line:80%
Odd.

00:34:51.684 --> 00:34:52.685 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:34:56.730 --> 00:34:57.731 line:80%
[sighs contentedly]

00:34:57.815 --> 00:34:59.608 line:80%
[cell phone pinging]

00:34:59.692 --> 00:35:01.819 line:80%
[grumbles] Who keeps messaging?

00:35:01.902 --> 00:35:03.320 line:80%
It's me.

00:35:03.904 --> 00:35:05.823 line:80%
I'm uploading our photos
to our group chat.

00:35:05.906 --> 00:35:07.324 line:80%
-[Raemee chuckles]
-[Sol] Oh…

00:35:08.534 --> 00:35:09.743 line:80%
[cell phone vibrates]

00:35:10.744 --> 00:35:13.372 line:80%
-[Sol] Mmm.
-Hi, Hayeong. Did you see…

00:35:15.791 --> 00:35:16.792 line:80%
[in English] What?

00:35:17.918 --> 00:35:19.420 line:80%
[in Korean] I'm not sure…

00:35:21.547 --> 00:35:23.632 line:80%
if I have the right to tell you

00:35:25.384 --> 00:35:26.719 line:80%
about myself.

00:35:27.928 --> 00:35:29.138 line:80%
To be honest…

00:35:33.350 --> 00:35:34.351 line:80%
I'm scared.

00:35:35.686 --> 00:35:38.981 line:80%
You asked me what happened in America.

00:35:40.649 --> 00:35:41.775 line:80%
I…

00:35:44.695 --> 00:35:45.821 line:80%
was actually…

00:35:50.367 --> 00:35:52.411 line:80%
in Boston, attending…

00:35:53.662 --> 00:35:54.663 line:80%
[exclaims]

00:35:56.165 --> 00:35:57.624 line:80%
[Hayeong] <i>Haran's a total lightweight.</i>

00:35:57.708 --> 00:35:59.084 line:80%
<i>She can't drink a single drop.</i>

00:35:59.168 --> 00:36:00.544 line:80%
<i>Don't let her drink anything.</i>

00:36:00.627 --> 00:36:03.339 line:80%
-[Raemee in English] Stop!
-[in Korean] She can't drink at all!

00:36:03.422 --> 00:36:05.341 line:80%
-Wait!
-Ms. Song!

00:36:05.966 --> 00:36:07.968 line:80%
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

00:36:22.691 --> 00:36:23.692 line:80%
[sighs softly]

00:36:25.903 --> 00:36:27.905 line:80%
[bells chiming in distance]

00:36:32.785 --> 00:36:33.786 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:36:40.834 --> 00:36:42.836 line:80%
[chiming continues]

00:36:44.546 --> 00:36:46.799 line:80%
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

00:36:51.428 --> 00:36:53.097 line:80%
[Hyeokchan] <i>Hey. Sorry, Haran.</i>

00:36:53.806 --> 00:36:54.974 line:80%
That song?

00:36:55.057 --> 00:36:57.017 line:80%
Okay, I'll listen to it.

00:36:57.101 --> 00:36:59.228 line:80%
Can you message her back?

00:36:59.311 --> 00:37:00.729 line:80%
Sorry. Do me a solid.

00:37:00.813 --> 00:37:02.856 line:80%
Anything that a woman
in her twenties can use.

00:37:02.940 --> 00:37:06.193 line:80%
I have to go to the hospital
because of my hand. [echoing]

00:37:14.535 --> 00:37:16.286 line:80%
-[shatters]
-[Hyeokchan groans, inhales sharply]

00:37:19.498 --> 00:37:21.208 line:80%
[Hyeokchan groans, inhales sharply]

00:37:21.291 --> 00:37:22.835 line:80%
[♪ music continues]

00:37:26.422 --> 00:37:28.507 line:80%
-[patient exclaims]
-[metallic clink echoing]

00:37:30.342 --> 00:37:31.468 line:80%
[in English] Sorry.

00:37:31.552 --> 00:37:34.722 line:80%
-[in Korean] Thanks, Chan.
-Who's that? Your friend?

00:37:34.805 --> 00:37:36.432 line:80%
[Hyeokchan] No, just my roommate.

00:37:38.809 --> 00:37:41.186 line:80%
Sorry, Ran. My professor's calling.

00:37:41.270 --> 00:37:42.521 line:80%
I'll call you back later.

00:37:44.064 --> 00:37:45.107 line:80%
Sujin. You're here?

00:37:45.607 --> 00:37:46.608 line:80%
I'll head out now.

00:37:49.194 --> 00:37:50.237 line:80%
I'll be away for a few weeks.

00:37:50.321 --> 00:37:53.115 line:80%
I'm traveling around the East Coast
during vacation.

00:37:53.907 --> 00:37:57.703 line:80%
If our professor asks for me,
say I'm taking a break because of my hand.

00:38:01.040 --> 00:38:03.667 line:80%
[clinking]

00:38:08.922 --> 00:38:10.716 line:80%
[clinking echoes]

00:38:10.799 --> 00:38:11.800 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:38:13.510 --> 00:38:15.429 line:80%
[metallic clink echoes]

00:38:15.512 --> 00:38:16.597 line:80%
[thud echoes]

00:38:16.680 --> 00:38:18.432 line:80%
[high-pitched ringing]

00:38:18.557 --> 00:38:20.559 line:80%
[♪ dramatic music playing]

00:38:23.562 --> 00:38:27.066 line:80%
[Haran] <i>Getting close to someone</i>
<i>is really difficult…</i>

00:38:27.149 --> 00:38:28.984 line:80%
<i>No, it's scary for me.</i>

00:38:29.860 --> 00:38:33.739 line:80%
[Haran vocalizing "Goldberg Variations,
BWV 988: Aria" by J.S. Bach on phone]

00:38:37.951 --> 00:38:41.330 line:80%
[♪ J.S. Bach "Goldberg Variations,
BWV 988: Aria" plays on earphones]

00:38:41.413 --> 00:38:43.624 line:80%
[Haran] <i>It's all thanks to this pen.</i>

00:38:43.707 --> 00:38:45.751 line:80%
It's really valuable to me,
so I have to find it.

00:38:45.834 --> 00:38:47.252 line:80%
[♪ dramatic music continues]

00:38:47.336 --> 00:38:49.171 line:80%
<i>Chan, I saw a vapor trail earlier.</i>

00:38:49.254 --> 00:38:52.091 line:80%
<i>But that made me want</i>
<i>to get on a plane to go see you.</i>

00:38:53.717 --> 00:38:55.928 line:80%
<i>Whether you're a guy or not,</i>
<i>I don't want to get close.</i>

00:39:02.101 --> 00:39:05.729 line:80%
-[♪ music climaxes, fades]
-[gasping]

00:39:05.813 --> 00:39:07.815 line:80%
[♪ dramatic music continues]

00:39:18.826 --> 00:39:21.120 line:80%
[breathing shakily]

00:39:27.459 --> 00:39:29.461 line:80%
[sobbing echoes]

00:39:39.471 --> 00:39:40.472 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:39:41.140 --> 00:39:42.141 line:80%
[gasps]

00:39:43.183 --> 00:39:44.893 line:80%
[exclaims softly, gasps]

00:39:46.687 --> 00:39:48.814 line:80%
It's morning?

00:39:50.149 --> 00:39:51.150 line:80%
[gasps]

00:39:58.991 --> 00:40:00.826 line:80%
-[floor creaks]
-[door slides shut]

00:40:01.410 --> 00:40:03.704 line:80%
Hey. You spoke as if you were
a heavy drinker,

00:40:03.787 --> 00:40:08.250 line:80%
but you passed out right away. [chuckles]

00:40:09.168 --> 00:40:13.630 line:80%
I don't usually pass out
after drinking like that,

00:40:13.714 --> 00:40:16.258 line:80%
but the alcohol tasted really good.

00:40:16.342 --> 00:40:20.095 line:80%
Maybe it was because the weather
was so nice. [chuckles awkwardly]

00:40:24.099 --> 00:40:25.184 line:80%
Hey, Sujin.

00:40:25.267 --> 00:40:26.727 line:80%
[metallic clink echoes]

00:40:28.979 --> 00:40:31.106 line:80%
It's okay to be a lightweight.

00:40:31.190 --> 00:40:32.858 line:80%
Why are you looking at me with pity?

00:40:32.941 --> 00:40:35.194 line:80%
No, I'm not looking at you that way.

00:40:35.277 --> 00:40:38.489 line:80%
You are. You just looked at me
like I was a lost puppy.

00:40:41.992 --> 00:40:42.993 line:80%
[Chan] Hmm.

00:40:44.536 --> 00:40:45.537 line:80%
[inhales sharply]

00:40:46.830 --> 00:40:49.667 line:80%
It's pitiful that
you're waiting for your old owner.

00:40:49.750 --> 00:40:52.586 line:80%
I should be good to you
so you won't remember them.

00:40:54.129 --> 00:40:55.798 line:80%
Is that how I looked at you?

00:40:57.007 --> 00:40:58.467 line:80%
No need to say it like that…

00:40:59.093 --> 00:41:01.053 line:80%
Let's go. Oh.

00:41:01.136 --> 00:41:03.305 line:80%
-Bring your jacket.
-Where are we going?

00:41:03.889 --> 00:41:05.599 line:80%
A hangover cure walk?

00:41:05.683 --> 00:41:08.644 line:80%
If walking cured hangovers,
hangover soup places would close down.

00:41:10.187 --> 00:41:13.691 line:80%
But when exactly did I pass out?

00:41:14.775 --> 00:41:15.943 line:80%
Don't you remember?

00:41:17.319 --> 00:41:18.487 line:80%
This.

00:41:22.116 --> 00:41:23.826 line:80%
Right. Odd or even.

00:41:24.410 --> 00:41:27.997 line:80%
[groans] I should have said odd.
Why did I guess even?

00:41:28.831 --> 00:41:31.375 line:80%
-You didn't…
-Let's just say I did.

00:41:32.626 --> 00:41:35.462 line:80%
There's no need to know everything.

00:41:35.546 --> 00:41:36.547 line:80%
Still…

00:41:36.630 --> 00:41:39.341 line:80%
You used your card
so you wouldn't have to tell me.

00:41:39.425 --> 00:41:41.260 line:80%
It must have been something bad.

00:41:41.927 --> 00:41:44.138 line:80%
I don't want to force you
to talk about it.

00:41:45.139 --> 00:41:48.559 line:80%
There's no need to dig into your scars
to learn more about you.

00:41:52.604 --> 00:41:54.732 line:80%
And even if I don't know about it,

00:41:55.649 --> 00:41:57.651 line:80%
we're already quite close, right?

00:42:03.657 --> 00:42:05.993 line:80%
[inhales sharply] Oh, right.

00:42:06.076 --> 00:42:07.328 line:80%
Here.

00:42:07.411 --> 00:42:08.537 line:80%
Honey water.

00:42:08.620 --> 00:42:10.664 line:80%
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

00:42:10.748 --> 00:42:14.168 line:80%
Hangover medicine, hangover drink,

00:42:14.251 --> 00:42:17.129 line:80%
-roasted eggs, and…
-[Haran gasps]

00:42:17.796 --> 00:42:19.673 line:80%
They must have been really kind to you.

00:42:20.215 --> 00:42:21.216 line:80%
Who?

00:42:21.300 --> 00:42:24.386 line:80%
The person who showed you
a way to keep going.

00:42:25.304 --> 00:42:26.805 line:80%
The one who kept reaching out.

00:42:27.931 --> 00:42:30.851 line:80%
I just wondered
if you're so sweet to other people

00:42:30.934 --> 00:42:33.395 line:80%
because you learned it from them.

00:42:36.398 --> 00:42:39.109 line:80%
[inhales sharply, sighs]

00:42:39.193 --> 00:42:41.153 line:80%
How should I say it…

00:42:41.779 --> 00:42:43.030 line:80%
I'm no match.

00:42:43.947 --> 00:42:46.158 line:80%
This is nothing
compared to what I received.

00:42:46.241 --> 00:42:48.452 line:80%
I received something so incredible

00:42:49.370 --> 00:42:50.829 line:80%
that I could never repay her.

00:42:52.998 --> 00:42:54.291 line:80%
Was it your girlfriend?

00:42:54.375 --> 00:42:57.378 line:80%
No, of course not. I wouldn't dare.

00:42:58.754 --> 00:43:00.964 line:80%
It wasn't like that. Mmm…

00:43:01.799 --> 00:43:02.800 line:80%
She was just…

00:43:04.343 --> 00:43:07.346 line:80%
someone who broadened my world.

00:43:08.013 --> 00:43:09.932 line:80%
Broadened your world?

00:43:10.015 --> 00:43:11.016 line:80%
Yes.

00:43:12.601 --> 00:43:14.478 line:80%
She let me experience things

00:43:15.813 --> 00:43:17.564 line:80%
that I couldn't see or feel before.

00:43:18.941 --> 00:43:22.903 line:80%
My world used to be
black and white, but she…

00:43:24.905 --> 00:43:26.782 line:80%
filled it with vibrant colors.

00:43:31.161 --> 00:43:32.955 line:80%
[inhales sharply] Right. High five!

00:43:33.580 --> 00:43:35.791 line:80%
I have a habit of doing high fives
when I'm grateful.

00:43:36.375 --> 00:43:38.210 line:80%
You're grateful? All of a sudden?

00:43:39.336 --> 00:43:40.546 line:80%
I found the answer.

00:43:41.672 --> 00:43:44.550 line:80%
My choice was filled with question marks,

00:43:45.092 --> 00:43:48.971 line:80%
but you just changed them
to exclamation marks.

00:43:50.514 --> 00:43:51.515 line:80%
Your choice?

00:43:51.598 --> 00:43:53.225 line:80%
I chose never to do anything

00:43:53.309 --> 00:43:57.187 line:80%
that might get in the way
of her happiness.

00:43:58.105 --> 00:44:00.524 line:80%
Thanks to you, I just realized

00:44:01.150 --> 00:44:04.695 line:80%
that not digging up old wounds
is also a way…

00:44:06.155 --> 00:44:08.532 line:80%
of protecting their happiness.

00:44:09.700 --> 00:44:11.243 line:80%
That's why I'm asking

00:44:11.994 --> 00:44:12.995 line:80%
for a high five.

00:44:13.871 --> 00:44:16.832 line:80%
Well, I have no idea
what you're talking about,

00:44:16.915 --> 00:44:18.959 line:80%
but since you say I helped…

00:44:19.710 --> 00:44:20.711 line:80%
[chuckles softly]

00:44:28.719 --> 00:44:29.720 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:44:29.803 --> 00:44:31.722 line:80%
[Hayeong retches] Two green onions…

00:44:34.099 --> 00:44:36.310 line:80%
[retches] Three green onions…

00:44:38.187 --> 00:44:39.855 line:80%
Isn't that for your hangover?

00:44:39.938 --> 00:44:42.316 line:80%
Why are you making art
instead of eating it?

00:44:42.399 --> 00:44:46.153 line:80%
I may be friendly with everyone,
but not green onions…

00:44:47.237 --> 00:44:49.531 line:80%
What? Hang on.

00:44:50.449 --> 00:44:51.450 line:80%
Mmm.

00:44:52.660 --> 00:44:54.828 line:80%
<i>He picked out the green onions for me.</i>

00:44:54.912 --> 00:44:57.081 line:80%
<i>How did he know I don't eat green onions?</i>

00:44:57.706 --> 00:45:00.626 line:80%
<i>Green onions… What does that mean?</i>

00:45:01.502 --> 00:45:02.836 line:80%
Did he flirt with green onions?

00:45:02.920 --> 00:45:04.546 line:80%
I'm heading out now.

00:45:04.630 --> 00:45:05.839 line:80%
Right, the tonics.

00:45:05.923 --> 00:45:10.010 line:80%
I should take a tonic
that Mr. Yeon gave me.

00:45:10.094 --> 00:45:11.387 line:80%
-Huh?
-[Nana] Oh.

00:45:11.470 --> 00:45:14.807 line:80%
I should take the vitamins
that Mr. Yeon got me.

00:45:14.890 --> 00:45:16.684 line:80%
-What?
-He seemed a bit reserved,

00:45:16.767 --> 00:45:18.185 line:80%
but he takes care of our whole family.

00:45:18.268 --> 00:45:20.062 line:80%
He's so thoughtful.

00:45:20.145 --> 00:45:22.439 line:80%
-I'll get going now.
-See you.

00:45:22.523 --> 00:45:23.899 line:80%
Okay.

00:45:25.109 --> 00:45:26.110 line:80%
[stutters] Grandma.

00:45:26.902 --> 00:45:31.448 line:80%
Did Mr. Yeon always
take care of everyone like this?

00:45:31.532 --> 00:45:33.283 line:80%
What's the point of having you three?

00:45:33.367 --> 00:45:35.369 line:80%
Mr. Yeon's the only one
who takes care of me.

00:45:37.830 --> 00:45:39.289 line:80%
Geez.

00:45:40.082 --> 00:45:42.251 line:80%
I was overreacting for no reason.

00:45:45.504 --> 00:45:46.505 line:80%
Gosh, that's hot.

00:45:46.588 --> 00:45:49.425 line:80%
-Great work.
-Great work, everyone.

00:45:49.508 --> 00:45:50.884 line:80%
-Thank you.
-[Sol] Great work.

00:45:50.968 --> 00:45:52.511 line:80%
[Ben] Thank you for everything.

00:45:53.846 --> 00:45:55.389 line:80%
I'll see you in Seoul.

00:45:55.472 --> 00:45:57.141 line:80%
Okay. I'll see you in 10 days.

00:45:57.683 --> 00:45:59.476 line:80%
Oh. That's a day for pizza.

00:45:59.560 --> 00:46:01.478 line:80%
How about pizza that day?

00:46:02.980 --> 00:46:04.982 line:80%
-Is it a full moon? [chuckles softly]
-Mmm.

00:46:05.065 --> 00:46:06.483 line:80%
Sure, pizza sounds good.

00:46:06.567 --> 00:46:08.485 line:80%
And here.

00:46:09.611 --> 00:46:11.322 line:80%
For the hangover stuff you gave me.

00:46:11.405 --> 00:46:12.990 line:80%
HANG IN THERE!

00:46:13.449 --> 00:46:15.451 line:80%
[chuckles softly] I also have…

00:46:16.702 --> 00:46:17.703 line:80%
this.

00:46:18.412 --> 00:46:19.413 line:80%
Hmm?

00:46:20.039 --> 00:46:21.040 line:80%
Homework.

00:46:21.874 --> 00:46:22.875 line:80%
[Haran] A film camera?

00:46:22.958 --> 00:46:24.418 line:80%
What kind of homework?

00:46:24.501 --> 00:46:26.211 line:80%
Well…

00:46:27.338 --> 00:46:29.340 line:80%
Ms. Song, hurry.

00:46:29.423 --> 00:46:30.507 line:80%
Come on.

00:46:31.550 --> 00:46:33.177 line:80%
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

00:46:33.761 --> 00:46:35.262 line:80%
Hurry!

00:46:37.431 --> 00:46:39.600 line:80%
It would be a huge waste not to see that.

00:46:42.645 --> 00:46:45.564 line:80%
-[Haran] Wow, it's beautiful.
-[camera clicks]

00:46:45.648 --> 00:46:47.733 line:80%
It's called an iridescent cloud.

00:46:48.692 --> 00:46:49.818 line:80%
An iridescent cloud?

00:46:49.902 --> 00:46:51.904 line:80%
[Chan] We also call them
mother-of-pearl clouds.

00:46:51.987 --> 00:46:55.199 line:80%
Because of the diffraction of sunlight,
the cloud particles…

00:46:55.282 --> 00:46:56.909 line:80%
Forget it.

00:46:57.493 --> 00:46:58.994 line:80%
It's a good omen.

00:46:59.078 --> 00:47:01.747 line:80%
They say you have good luck
if you see an iridescent cloud.

00:47:02.831 --> 00:47:04.249 line:80%
That's childish.

00:47:05.542 --> 00:47:07.044 line:80%
Do people say it's lucky?

00:47:08.837 --> 00:47:10.089 line:80%
[chuckles]

00:47:10.172 --> 00:47:12.049 line:80%
-[camera clicks]
-Wait, it's blurry.

00:47:13.634 --> 00:47:14.635 line:80%
[inhales deeply]

00:47:15.344 --> 00:47:19.765 line:80%
You should look for iridescent clouds
in the sky, too,

00:47:19.848 --> 00:47:21.517 line:80%
instead of just vapor trails.

00:47:23.310 --> 00:47:24.311 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:47:24.395 --> 00:47:29.149 line:80%
Vapor trails are just traces
of something that already passed by.

00:47:29.942 --> 00:47:33.529 line:80%
But iridescent clouds
make you excited for the future.

00:47:33.612 --> 00:47:34.613 line:80%
[♪ music continues]

00:47:34.697 --> 00:47:35.948 line:80%
The past…

00:47:37.700 --> 00:47:41.328 line:80%
may not be as beautiful as you remember.

00:47:41.870 --> 00:47:44.581 line:80%
They get blurred,
overwritten, and distorted.

00:47:45.749 --> 00:47:49.253 line:80%
Or they may have been romanticized
because some things…

00:47:50.254 --> 00:47:51.547 line:80%
were hidden.

00:47:53.674 --> 00:47:55.592 line:80%
Why are you suddenly saying that?

00:47:55.676 --> 00:47:56.677 line:80%
I was just…

00:47:57.678 --> 00:48:00.764 line:80%
worried that you'd miss
an iridescent cloud

00:48:00.848 --> 00:48:02.141 line:80%
while staring at a vapor trail.

00:48:03.600 --> 00:48:06.603 line:80%
I have a habit of feeling upset
if I miss something exciting

00:48:06.687 --> 00:48:09.189 line:80%
while thinking about the past.
[chuckles softly]

00:48:10.065 --> 00:48:11.066 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:48:11.191 --> 00:48:12.901 line:80%
[Raemee] All right, everybody. Come here!

00:48:12.985 --> 00:48:14.987 line:80%
-Ending a trip…
-With a group photo…

00:48:15.070 --> 00:48:17.573 line:80%
[group] ...is a must!

00:48:17.656 --> 00:48:18.824 line:80%
Let's go.

00:48:18.907 --> 00:48:21.327 line:80%
-[♪ pleasant music playing]
-[lively chatter]

00:48:21.410 --> 00:48:25.414 line:80%
[indistinct chatter]

00:48:25.497 --> 00:48:27.541 line:80%
[Sol] All right. Here goes.

00:48:27.624 --> 00:48:28.834 line:80%
[Raemee] Hurry.

00:48:28.917 --> 00:48:31.045 line:80%
Okay, everyone. What's one plus one?

00:48:31.128 --> 00:48:34.006 line:80%
-[all] Two!
-[in English] Two!

00:48:36.592 --> 00:48:38.802 line:80%
[♪ uplifting song playing]

00:48:56.111 --> 00:48:57.696 line:80%
[Haran] <i>But what sort of homework is this?</i>

00:48:57.780 --> 00:48:59.323 line:80%
Take one photo each day

00:48:59.406 --> 00:49:01.367 line:80%
and show them to me
when I return to Seoul.

00:49:01.450 --> 00:49:03.494 line:80%
Isn't it crazy, though?

00:49:03.577 --> 00:49:06.205 line:80%
How did they know I'm leaving in 10 days

00:49:06.288 --> 00:49:08.832 line:80%
and sell a 10-shot camera?
[chuckles softly]

00:49:08.916 --> 00:49:10.876 line:80%
What should I take photos of?

00:49:10.959 --> 00:49:13.879 line:80%
Something fun, delicious, or pretty.

00:49:13.962 --> 00:49:17.633 line:80%
Just anything
that made you feel good that day.

00:49:30.145 --> 00:49:31.897 line:80%
[Haran] <i>Hang in there!</i>

00:49:37.987 --> 00:49:39.029 line:80%
[sighs contentedly]

00:49:45.911 --> 00:49:46.912 line:80%
[♪ song fades]

00:49:47.830 --> 00:49:50.666 line:80%
-I'd like some coffee.
-It's on me, so help yourselves!

00:49:50.749 --> 00:49:52.960 line:80%
-[Sol] This is so good!
-I got us some coffee.

00:49:53.043 --> 00:49:54.211 line:80%
[Seunggyu] What's with the coffee?

00:49:54.294 --> 00:49:57.464 line:80%
I heard Je Raemee was bringing
Gyeongju bread today.

00:49:57.548 --> 00:49:59.299 line:80%
I thought it would go well with coffee.

00:49:59.383 --> 00:50:00.509 line:80%
Can I have one?

00:50:01.593 --> 00:50:02.928 line:80%
Wasn't Gyeongju amazing?

00:50:03.012 --> 00:50:07.474 line:80%
There were so many things to see and eat,
and the beach was so beautiful…

00:50:09.059 --> 00:50:10.352 line:80%
What is it?

00:50:10.436 --> 00:50:14.106 line:80%
We've never seen you talk for so long
about something other than work.

00:50:14.189 --> 00:50:16.191 line:80%
It's the first time since I joined.

00:50:17.860 --> 00:50:19.486 line:80%
[♪ whimsical music playing]

00:50:19.570 --> 00:50:21.447 line:80%
Let's start working, then.

00:50:26.577 --> 00:50:28.412 line:80%
[scoffs] She's suddenly
acting so friendly.

00:50:29.204 --> 00:50:32.750 line:80%
Well, she's not tinting her windows
or brooding like before.

00:50:32.833 --> 00:50:36.670 line:80%
I guess she's a tiny bit… better
than before.

00:50:36.754 --> 00:50:37.755 line:80%
[elevator dings]

00:50:39.048 --> 00:50:41.383 line:80%
-Hello.
-[buttons beep]

00:50:42.009 --> 00:50:45.763 line:80%
[inhales sharply, grunts]

00:50:45.846 --> 00:50:47.097 line:80%
[yawns]

00:50:48.557 --> 00:50:51.268 line:80%
Wow. You and sweet and sour candy?

00:50:51.894 --> 00:50:53.270 line:80%
That really doesn't suit you.

00:50:53.354 --> 00:50:56.315 line:80%
Ah. I guess you're giving it to someone.

00:50:57.149 --> 00:50:58.150 line:80%
Pardon?

00:50:58.734 --> 00:51:00.694 line:80%
Would you like one?

00:51:01.278 --> 00:51:02.446 line:80%
Sure.

00:51:02.946 --> 00:51:04.782 line:80%
-[elevator dings]
-I'll try one, then.

00:51:06.158 --> 00:51:07.242 line:80%
Thank you.

00:51:09.328 --> 00:51:10.412 line:80%
[hums delightedly]

00:51:11.372 --> 00:51:12.790 line:80%
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

00:51:23.050 --> 00:51:24.051 line:80%
Hello.

00:51:24.134 --> 00:51:26.845 line:80%
I'm Yeon Taeseok
from Seoul Commercial High School.

00:51:26.929 --> 00:51:29.807 line:80%
[exclaims] Mr. Yeon Taeseok.

00:51:29.890 --> 00:51:31.976 line:80%
Even your name sounds proper.

00:51:32.935 --> 00:51:35.020 line:80%
But you said hello to the wrong person.

00:51:35.521 --> 00:51:37.898 line:80%
Oh… Sorry.

00:51:37.982 --> 00:51:40.609 line:80%
[stutters] No need to apologize.

00:51:41.110 --> 00:51:44.488 line:80%
Wow. You're sweating a lot.

00:51:45.614 --> 00:51:47.282 line:80%
[chuckles] Ah.

00:51:48.826 --> 00:51:50.244 line:80%
Would you like one?

00:51:50.327 --> 00:51:51.412 line:80%
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

00:51:51.495 --> 00:51:53.914 line:80%
The sour taste will snap you awake,

00:51:53.998 --> 00:51:55.958 line:80%
and the sweet taste will help you relax.

00:51:56.834 --> 00:51:59.586 line:80%
Eat that to relax your nerves.

00:51:59.670 --> 00:52:00.796 line:80%
Thank you.

00:52:00.879 --> 00:52:01.880 line:80%
And…

00:52:02.506 --> 00:52:04.425 line:80%
There's a piece of tissue here.

00:52:05.134 --> 00:52:07.928 line:80%
[chuckles softly] Then good luck.

00:52:08.012 --> 00:52:10.097 line:80%
-You can do it.
-Right.

00:52:11.765 --> 00:52:12.933 line:80%
[sighs]

00:52:13.017 --> 00:52:15.894 line:80%
I tried to get some pocket money
from Grandma but got a noogie.

00:52:23.027 --> 00:52:24.111 line:80%
[exhales]

00:52:24.737 --> 00:52:27.906 line:80%
Mr. Yeon Taeseok,
Ms. Kim will see you now.

00:52:27.990 --> 00:52:28.991 line:80%
Okay.

00:52:38.083 --> 00:52:39.168 line:80%
[softly] Thank you.

00:52:44.048 --> 00:52:45.049 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:52:45.132 --> 00:52:46.550 line:80%
[indistinct chatter]

00:52:48.594 --> 00:52:49.636 line:80%
I'll be right back.

00:52:50.137 --> 00:52:51.347 line:80%
Hadam!

00:52:55.893 --> 00:52:57.936 line:80%
Are you going to your math academy?

00:52:58.604 --> 00:53:00.439 line:80%
What is it?

00:53:00.522 --> 00:53:02.399 line:80%
You look worried about something.

00:53:03.776 --> 00:53:06.695 line:80%
What is it?
Tell your boyfriend everything.

00:53:08.489 --> 00:53:09.782 line:80%
Yougyum.

00:53:12.034 --> 00:53:15.162 line:80%
Did you go to a jewelry shop
a few days ago…

00:53:15.245 --> 00:53:16.705 line:80%
-[players exclaim teasingly]
-Hey, Yougyum!

00:53:16.789 --> 00:53:20.042 line:80%
Enough with the PDA and get back here.
We have to practice.

00:53:20.709 --> 00:53:23.212 line:80%
Go on. We'll talk later.

00:53:23.295 --> 00:53:25.422 line:80%
I'll call you later.

00:53:25.506 --> 00:53:27.424 line:80%
[♪ amusing music playing]

00:53:30.094 --> 00:53:33.305 line:80%
If anything is bothering you, tell me.
I'll take care of everything…

00:53:33.389 --> 00:53:36.016 line:80%
I mean, everything besides studying.

00:53:36.100 --> 00:53:38.644 line:80%
[giggles] All right.

00:53:39.728 --> 00:53:41.730 line:80%
Hang in there! [giggles]

00:53:43.565 --> 00:53:45.985 line:80%
[scoffs] Park Yeseul…

00:53:46.068 --> 00:53:48.862 line:80%
Why did she have to bring up
Han Sora? [chuckles softly]

00:53:49.947 --> 00:53:52.032 line:80%
[cell phone vibrating]

00:53:52.116 --> 00:53:53.701 line:80%
CHA YOUGYUM

00:53:55.869 --> 00:53:58.163 line:80%
SORA

00:53:58.247 --> 00:53:59.248 line:80%
-[vibrating]
-[♪ music ends]

00:54:00.290 --> 00:54:01.333 line:80%
Yes, Ms. Kim.

00:54:02.960 --> 00:54:04.336 line:80%
The revised sketch?

00:54:05.004 --> 00:54:07.006 line:80%
No. I'll hand it in by today.

00:54:08.465 --> 00:54:09.550 line:80%
Okay.

00:54:11.135 --> 00:54:12.136 line:80%
[line disconnects]

00:54:13.012 --> 00:54:16.265 line:80%
[groans] I really need an idea. Please…

00:54:16.348 --> 00:54:18.350 line:80%
-[whines]
-[cell phone buzzes]

00:54:20.185 --> 00:54:21.395 line:80%
[sighs exasperatedly]

00:54:22.771 --> 00:54:24.898 line:80%
[Chan] <i>I'm sending you a photo</i>
<i>since you said yours was blurry.</i>

00:54:30.321 --> 00:54:31.613 line:80%
[chuckles softly]

00:54:32.323 --> 00:54:33.324 line:80%
[knock on door]

00:54:33.407 --> 00:54:35.534 line:80%
Ms. Song, the material check…

00:54:36.201 --> 00:54:39.204 line:80%
[gasps loudly] What happened to your hair?

00:54:39.955 --> 00:54:43.125 line:80%
Whoa. What's that? The colors are amazing.

00:54:43.208 --> 00:54:47.004 line:80%
I saw it for the first time in Gyeongju.
It's called an iridescent cloud.

00:54:47.087 --> 00:54:48.339 line:80%
[Sol] It's a cloud?

00:54:48.422 --> 00:54:50.007 line:80%
Wow. It looks like a rainbow.

00:54:50.090 --> 00:54:52.051 line:80%
They call it a rainbow cloud, too.

00:54:52.676 --> 00:54:54.470 line:80%
It's also called a mother-of-pearl cloud…

00:54:55.888 --> 00:54:57.514 line:80%
because of the color…

00:54:57.598 --> 00:54:58.932 line:80%
[♪ pleasant music playing]

00:55:02.728 --> 00:55:06.398 line:80%
-Oh. Can you get my rolling cart?
-What?

00:55:07.441 --> 00:55:08.484 line:80%
Right.

00:55:20.204 --> 00:55:21.205 line:80%
[sniffs]

00:55:38.347 --> 00:55:40.099 line:80%
<i>Here's the revised outfit design.</i>

00:55:40.683 --> 00:55:42.309 line:80%
Sorry, I'm late.

00:55:50.567 --> 00:55:52.611 line:80%
-It wasn't just a simple revision.
-[♪ music ends]

00:55:52.695 --> 00:55:56.824 line:80%
The color was important,
so I made a colored illustration.

00:55:56.907 --> 00:55:59.493 line:80%
That's a color palette
I haven't seen before.

00:55:59.576 --> 00:56:03.872 line:80%
I applied mother-of-pearl colors
on the basic silhouette.

00:56:03.956 --> 00:56:06.625 line:80%
Mother-of-pearl…

00:56:06.709 --> 00:56:08.627 line:80%
-As in shiny seashells?
-Yes.

00:56:08.711 --> 00:56:13.424 line:80%
I thought it could be a great material
to highlight a Korean aesthetic.

00:56:13.507 --> 00:56:17.511 line:80%
For now, I just expressed
the general vibe with gloss pens,

00:56:17.594 --> 00:56:20.306 line:80%
but if we can capture
the texture of mother-of-pearl

00:56:20.389 --> 00:56:22.766 line:80%
so it has a mysterious glow
whenever she moves,

00:56:22.850 --> 00:56:25.728 line:80%
I think that would add some fun
to the animation as well.

00:56:25.811 --> 00:56:27.062 line:80%
Well…

00:56:27.146 --> 00:56:28.314 line:80%
Not bad.

00:56:28.856 --> 00:56:30.816 line:80%
Mother-of-pearl is normally used
for decorations.

00:56:31.400 --> 00:56:33.360 line:80%
How did you come up with the idea
of using its colors?

00:56:33.444 --> 00:56:34.445 line:80%
Oh…

00:56:35.321 --> 00:56:38.365 line:80%
This is an iridescent cloud
I saw in Gyeongju.

00:56:38.449 --> 00:56:40.784 line:80%
This photo became a great inspiration.

00:56:40.868 --> 00:56:43.412 line:80%
I heard it's also called
a mother-of-pearl cloud

00:56:43.495 --> 00:56:44.538 line:80%
because of its colors.

00:56:44.621 --> 00:56:45.873 line:80%
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

00:56:45.956 --> 00:56:47.124 line:80%
[Nana] Mmm.

00:56:47.207 --> 00:56:52.296 line:80%
It will go well with Raemee's idea
of emphasizing the collar and front panel.

00:56:54.840 --> 00:56:56.133 line:80%
So that trip wasn't for nothing.

00:56:57.801 --> 00:56:59.011 line:80%
You can go.

00:57:00.220 --> 00:57:01.388 line:80%
Okay.

00:57:06.352 --> 00:57:07.353 line:80%
[sighs]

00:57:09.605 --> 00:57:11.190 line:80%
She won't need me anymore.

00:57:14.026 --> 00:57:15.277 line:80%
-[cell phone buzzes]
-Hmm?

00:57:16.236 --> 00:57:17.821 line:80%
[Haran] <i>My sketch finally got accepted.</i>

00:57:23.702 --> 00:57:25.704 line:80%
Huh? Wait.

00:57:25.788 --> 00:57:27.915 line:20%
<i>Was this inspired</i>
<i>by that iridescent cloud?</i>

00:57:27.998 --> 00:57:31.168 line:20%
[Haran] <i>That's right. You said it's also</i>
<i>called a mother-of-pearl cloud.</i>

00:57:31.835 --> 00:57:34.213 line:20%
<i>It's all thanks to you.</i>
<i>I'll treat you to 10 pizzas.</i>

00:57:37.800 --> 00:57:39.385 line:80%
[inhales sharply] Let's see…

00:57:51.522 --> 00:57:53.524 line:80%
Mmm… [sighs]

00:57:54.984 --> 00:57:57.653 line:20%
[Chan] <i>They say you have good luck</i>
<i>if you see an iridescent cloud.</i>

00:57:58.362 --> 00:58:00.447 line:80%
-He was right.
-[♪ music fades]

00:58:00.531 --> 00:58:03.659 line:80%
[sighs in relief] It worked out
thanks to him. [chuckles softly]

00:58:05.285 --> 00:58:06.662 line:80%
The cloud you saw in Gyeongju?

00:58:07.579 --> 00:58:11.542 line:80%
[inhales deeply] Why do I feel like
I know who you saw it with?

00:58:11.625 --> 00:58:12.626 line:80%
What?

00:58:12.710 --> 00:58:17.548 line:80%
The Haran before wasn't my style,
so she was about 0.5 points,

00:58:17.631 --> 00:58:20.384 line:80%
but the new Song Haran
after our Gyeongju trip… Tsk.

00:58:20.884 --> 00:58:22.261 line:80%
Right, I'll give you three points.

00:58:22.886 --> 00:58:24.555 line:80%
Fine. I'll give you 3.5.

00:58:25.472 --> 00:58:27.391 line:80%
-Excuse me?
-Don't get too excited.

00:58:27.474 --> 00:58:28.809 line:80%
My points…

00:58:29.601 --> 00:58:31.520 line:80%
are out of 10.

00:58:31.603 --> 00:58:33.314 line:80%
[♪ amusing music plays]

00:58:38.652 --> 00:58:40.029 line:80%
All right.

00:58:48.412 --> 00:58:51.498 line:80%
[inhales sharply]
Didn't I tell you to stop coming?

00:58:57.963 --> 00:58:59.173 line:80%
[Yougyum] It's grated yam.

00:58:59.256 --> 00:59:01.342 line:80%
I did some research,
and they said it helps.

00:59:01.842 --> 00:59:04.386 line:80%
I'm already taking good care of myself.

00:59:04.470 --> 00:59:06.972 line:80%
Just focus on baseball.

00:59:07.056 --> 00:59:09.808 line:80%
I'm practicing really hard too, you know.

00:59:11.435 --> 00:59:14.396 line:80%
But what about
that examination you mentioned last time?

00:59:14.480 --> 00:59:15.481 line:80%
It's next week.

00:59:16.357 --> 00:59:18.859 line:80%
Are you getting along well with Hadam?

00:59:18.942 --> 00:59:21.195 line:80%
Why aren't you talking
about marriage anymore?

00:59:21.278 --> 00:59:25.199 line:80%
I decided to support her quietly
until the CSAT so I wouldn't distract her.

00:59:25.783 --> 00:59:27.910 line:80%
Have you been wearing
that necklace I gave you?

00:59:27.993 --> 00:59:29.995 line:80%
If it's not the right length, I can…

00:59:30.079 --> 00:59:31.372 line:80%
GUARDIAN

00:59:32.206 --> 00:59:34.500 line:80%
You're just a student.
Where did you get the money?

00:59:34.583 --> 00:59:37.169 line:80%
I'm a future Major Leaguer, you know.

00:59:37.252 --> 00:59:40.547 line:80%
Gosh. I should get
an autograph in advance.

00:59:40.631 --> 00:59:41.757 line:80%
[both chuckle]

00:59:43.300 --> 00:59:46.762 line:80%
Huh? Did you hit your leg somewhere?

00:59:47.346 --> 00:59:49.765 line:80%
It's fine. I just fell.

00:59:50.516 --> 00:59:52.434 line:80%
My legs suddenly wouldn't listen.

00:59:56.897 --> 01:00:00.609 line:80%
You have to make sure
Hadam doesn't find out until the CSAT.

01:00:02.695 --> 01:00:06.323 line:80%
Okay. I'll take good care of her.

01:00:08.867 --> 01:00:09.868 line:80%
[chuckles softly]

01:00:11.662 --> 01:00:13.288 line:80%
[cell phone vibrating]

01:00:18.585 --> 01:00:20.921 line:80%
-Hello?
-Are you free next next Friday at 7 p.m.?

01:00:21.005 --> 01:00:22.881 line:80%
Next next Friday?

01:00:24.008 --> 01:00:26.218 line:80%
-Well, yes…
-Okay.

01:00:26.301 --> 01:00:30.014 line:80%
Then let's have dinner at Samcheong-dong.

01:00:30.097 --> 01:00:31.307 line:80%
Samcheong-dong?

01:00:32.558 --> 01:00:35.394 line:80%
[Chan] <i>It's a one-table restaurant</i>
<i>I booked before coming to Korea.</i>

01:00:35.477 --> 01:00:36.937 line:20%
<i>Maybe it's thanks to that cloud.</i>

01:00:37.021 --> 01:00:38.480 line:20%
<i>There was a long waitlist,</i>

01:00:38.564 --> 01:00:41.400 line:20%
<i>but I just got a call</i>
<i>that someone canceled for that day.</i>

01:00:41.483 --> 01:00:43.277 line:80%
-Mmm.
-[Chan] <i>I'll send you the link.</i>

01:00:43.360 --> 01:00:44.862 line:80%
I haven't seen this place before.

01:00:45.529 --> 01:00:46.822 line:80%
[Chan] <i>I confirmed the reservation.</i>

01:00:46.905 --> 01:00:49.116 line:80%
<i>Ah. Mark that on your schedule.</i>

01:00:49.199 --> 01:00:51.201 line:80%
<i>You'd better not forget or show up late.</i>

01:00:51.285 --> 01:00:53.287 line:80%
[♪ pleasant song playing]

01:00:54.913 --> 01:00:56.874 line:80%
[gasps] I got distracted.

01:01:03.005 --> 01:01:04.006 line:80%
[sighs]

01:01:05.382 --> 01:01:06.842 line:80%
[waves splashing]

01:01:10.137 --> 01:01:12.097 line:80%
[talking indistinctly]

01:01:17.394 --> 01:01:19.438 line:80%
[Chan] <i>Good morning. Did you sleep well?</i>

01:01:19.980 --> 01:01:22.983 line:80%
<i>Our team did a sunrise shoot,</i>
<i>so everyone's knocked out now.</i>

01:01:23.984 --> 01:01:25.277 line:80%
Hey, a flower bloomed.

01:01:26.236 --> 01:01:29.281 line:80%
<i>But why aren't you sleeping?</i>
<i>Aren't you tired?</i>

01:01:30.032 --> 01:01:31.742 line:80%
[Chan] <i>I have to enjoy every moment.</i>

01:01:32.326 --> 01:01:34.912 line:80%
<i>Ah. There's a beautiful half-moon.</i>

01:01:35.746 --> 01:01:37.373 line:80%
<i>Can you see it clearly in Seoul?</i>

01:01:40.626 --> 01:01:42.252 line:80%
[Haran] <i>Yes, I can.</i>

01:01:45.756 --> 01:01:48.175 line:80%
<i>So today's dinner is omurice.</i>

01:01:50.594 --> 01:01:51.595 line:80%
[♪ song continues]

01:01:56.517 --> 01:01:57.518 line:80%
Donggu?

01:01:58.352 --> 01:02:01.105 line:80%
-Hello.
-Hi. [chuckles]

01:02:07.528 --> 01:02:11.240 line:80%
<i>What did you draw that character</i>
<i>on Donggu's uniform with?</i>

01:02:11.323 --> 01:02:13.283 line:80%
<i>A fabric marker?</i>

01:02:13.367 --> 01:02:14.618 line:80%
-That's right. [groans]
-[gasps]

01:02:17.579 --> 01:02:18.580 line:80%
[groans]

01:02:19.748 --> 01:02:22.418 line:20%
<i>Right. Mr. Park's checkup is on Wednesday.</i>

01:02:22.501 --> 01:02:24.294 line:80%
<i>Can you check up on him?</i>

01:02:25.295 --> 01:02:26.630 line:80%
Mr. Park.

01:02:26.714 --> 01:02:28.257 line:80%
Hey, you're here.

01:02:28.340 --> 01:02:29.383 line:80%
Genius.

01:02:29.466 --> 01:02:30.509 line:80%
-[chuckles]
-[camera shutter clicks]

01:02:31.802 --> 01:02:32.803 line:20%
[♪ music fades]

01:02:32.886 --> 01:02:35.055 line:80%
You didn't forget your checkup, right?

01:02:35.139 --> 01:02:38.726 line:80%
There's someone
calling me every day to remind me,

01:02:38.809 --> 01:02:40.978 line:80%
so I remember it
more clearly than my own birthday.

01:02:41.061 --> 01:02:42.563 line:80%
[Manjae chuckles]

01:02:42.646 --> 01:02:45.065 line:80%
But have you started a new hobby?

01:02:45.149 --> 01:02:46.817 line:80%
You've been taking a lot of photos.

01:02:47.401 --> 01:02:50.112 line:80%
Ah. Someone gave me homework,

01:02:50.195 --> 01:02:52.448 line:80%
telling me to take photos
of what makes me happy.

01:02:52.531 --> 01:02:55.492 line:80%
Mmm. So what did you take photos of?

01:02:55.576 --> 01:02:57.161 line:80%
Nothing special.

01:02:57.244 --> 01:02:58.871 line:80%
Just people around me,

01:02:58.954 --> 01:03:02.166 line:80%
the moon, delicious food,

01:03:02.249 --> 01:03:03.834 line:80%
that flower… Things like that.

01:03:03.917 --> 01:03:05.294 line:80%
Oh.

01:03:05.377 --> 01:03:08.422 line:80%
[sighs] I'm so curious how they'll look.
[chuckles softly]

01:03:08.505 --> 01:03:12.051 line:80%
They say happiness is always there,
but you just miss it,

01:03:12.676 --> 01:03:16.096 line:80%
so it belongs to the person
who discovers it.

01:03:16.180 --> 01:03:17.306 line:80%
I guess it's true.

01:03:18.140 --> 01:03:20.351 line:80%
I went on a walk with Genius earlier,

01:03:20.934 --> 01:03:22.978 line:80%
and the sky was so beautiful.

01:03:23.062 --> 01:03:24.938 line:80%
But no one even looked up.

01:03:25.689 --> 01:03:29.568 line:80%
They were all walking around,
staring at their phones.

01:03:29.652 --> 01:03:30.653 line:80%
[chuckles]

01:03:32.237 --> 01:03:34.239 line:80%
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

01:03:45.668 --> 01:03:47.252 line:80%
[Manjae] <i>I have a feeling</i>

01:03:47.336 --> 01:03:50.214 line:80%
<i>that the person who gave you that camera…</i>

01:03:50.297 --> 01:03:51.298 line:80%
[Chan inhales sharply]

01:03:51.382 --> 01:03:54.093 line:80%
[Manjae] <i>...is someone who knows</i>
<i>how to look up at the sky</i>

01:03:54.176 --> 01:03:55.844 line:80%
<i>on days like this.</i>

01:03:57.554 --> 01:04:00.432 line:80%
I guess that's why
they gave you that homework.

01:04:01.141 --> 01:04:06.313 line:80%
So you can discover nice things every day,
no matter how trivial they are.

01:04:06.397 --> 01:04:10.275 line:80%
They probably wanted you
to smile at least once while doing so.

01:04:10.359 --> 01:04:12.653 line:80%
Isn't that right? [chuckles]

01:04:19.410 --> 01:04:21.412 line:80%
Mr. Park, I think I get it now.

01:04:21.870 --> 01:04:22.871 line:80%
What?

01:04:22.955 --> 01:04:26.667 line:80%
I was surprised at how different I was
these days, but I didn't know why.

01:04:26.750 --> 01:04:30.421 line:80%
I guess that's because
it's been such a long time since I saw it.

01:04:31.338 --> 01:04:33.215 line:80%
Saw what?

01:04:34.675 --> 01:04:35.759 line:80%
Myself.

01:04:37.886 --> 01:04:40.597 line:80%
My past self.

01:04:41.265 --> 01:04:42.308 line:80%
[♪ music continues]

01:04:42.391 --> 01:04:43.559 line:80%
[Chan exclaims]

01:04:43.642 --> 01:04:45.436 line:80%
[Haran chuckles]

01:04:45.519 --> 01:04:48.480 line:80%
<i>I used to be able to find happiness</i>
<i>in the smallest things.</i>

01:04:48.564 --> 01:04:49.732 line:80%
[exclaims nervously]

01:04:49.815 --> 01:04:52.401 line:80%
<i>It's been a while since I saw</i>
<i>that side of me.</i>

01:04:52.484 --> 01:04:55.612 line:80%
[laughing, exclaiming]

01:04:55.696 --> 01:04:58.574 line:80%
<i>I was able to see it again</i>
<i>thanks to someone.</i>

01:04:59.533 --> 01:05:01.243 line:80%
<i>I guess that's why I was surprised.</i>

01:05:05.497 --> 01:05:07.583 line:80%
Mmm. [chuckles]

01:05:09.126 --> 01:05:10.294 line:80%
Oh, my.

01:05:11.253 --> 01:05:14.131 line:80%
The moon is beautiful.

01:05:14.214 --> 01:05:15.215 line:80%
[sighs contentedly]

01:05:15.966 --> 01:05:17.843 line:80%
I hope I can see a full moon soon.

01:05:19.094 --> 01:05:20.304 line:80%
[Manjae chuckles]

01:05:23.641 --> 01:05:24.642 line:80%
[sighs]

01:05:29.396 --> 01:05:30.898 line:80%
-[♪ music fades]
-[camera shutter clicks]

01:05:33.108 --> 01:05:34.109 line:80%
[chuckles softly]

01:05:38.822 --> 01:05:40.616 line:80%
Where can I find a photo studio?

01:05:46.080 --> 01:05:48.624 line:80%
[in English] Remember, we're stopping
at the rest area halfway, okay?

01:05:48.707 --> 01:05:49.833 line:80%
-Okay.
-See you later, bro!

01:05:49.917 --> 01:05:51.752 line:80%
-Okay. See you guys.
-Drive safely. See you.

01:05:51.835 --> 01:05:52.836 line:80%
Sorry, Ben.

01:05:52.920 --> 01:05:53.962 line:80%
[in Korean] Take a different car.

01:05:54.046 --> 01:05:56.048 line:80%
[in English] I'm going straight to Seoul.

01:05:56.131 --> 01:05:57.675 line:80%
[Ben in Korean]
But it's at least four hours.

01:05:57.758 --> 01:06:00.094 line:80%
-Bye.
-Hey, don't strain yourself.

01:06:00.177 --> 01:06:01.595 line:80%
I'll drive.

01:06:01.679 --> 01:06:03.514 line:80%
Huh? I said I'll drive.

01:06:03.597 --> 01:06:05.724 line:80%
It's fine. I'll see you in Seoul.

01:06:05.808 --> 01:06:07.643 line:80%
-Hey!
-I'm fine, Ben.

01:06:07.726 --> 01:06:10.688 line:80%
Seonu Chan! Drive slowly, okay?

01:06:11.355 --> 01:06:12.356 line:80%
[sighs]

01:06:13.649 --> 01:06:15.401 line:80%
[in English] He really
shouldn't be driving.

01:06:16.151 --> 01:06:18.153 line:80%
[♪ upbeat music playing]

01:06:23.117 --> 01:06:24.910 line:80%
[Chan in Korean]
<i>I'll arrive around 6:30 p.m.</i>

01:06:25.869 --> 01:06:27.121 line:80%
<i>Find a nice pizza place for us.</i>

01:06:27.204 --> 01:06:28.288 line:80%
[Haran] <i>See you later.</i>

01:06:41.760 --> 01:06:43.804 line:80%
ETA
1 HOUR

01:06:45.139 --> 01:06:46.348 line:80%
One hour.

01:06:47.224 --> 01:06:49.310 line:80%
[engine revving]

01:06:49.393 --> 01:06:51.061 line:20%
-[cell phone vibrating]
-[♪ music ends]

01:06:52.479 --> 01:06:53.564 line:80%
[♪ tense music playing]

01:06:53.647 --> 01:06:56.025 line:80%
[cell phone continues vibrating]

01:07:01.405 --> 01:07:02.489 line:80%
[truck horn blares]

01:07:02.573 --> 01:07:03.615 line:80%
-[exclaims]
-[tires screech]

01:07:03.699 --> 01:07:05.117 line:80%
[cell phone vibrating]

01:07:06.076 --> 01:07:07.494 line:80%
Oh? Has he arrived early?

01:07:11.832 --> 01:07:14.126 line:80%
-Yes, Ms. Kim.
-[Nana] <i>Come to my office.</i>

01:07:15.127 --> 01:07:16.545 line:20%
18:04
MS. KIM

01:07:17.629 --> 01:07:18.839 line:80%
Right now?

01:07:19.715 --> 01:07:20.716 line:80%
[line disconnects]

01:07:24.845 --> 01:07:26.180 line:80%
Me?

01:07:26.263 --> 01:07:28.223 line:80%
Yes, you. Who else?

01:07:28.307 --> 01:07:30.559 line:80%
Why would you make me handle the business?

01:07:30.643 --> 01:07:33.729 line:80%
I'm retiring later than planned,
and you held on longer than I thought.

01:07:33.812 --> 01:07:34.855 line:80%
It's time you took over.

01:07:35.981 --> 01:07:37.608 line:80%
I didn't get to go at 60 as I planned,

01:07:37.691 --> 01:07:39.943 line:80%
but I'm going to retire soon
and go to France.

01:07:40.527 --> 01:07:41.528 line:80%
So start preparing.

01:07:42.237 --> 01:07:44.615 line:80%
No, I can't do this.

01:07:44.698 --> 01:07:48.202 line:80%
I'm already overwhelmed with doing design,
and I'm not qualified…

01:07:48.285 --> 01:07:49.870 line:80%
You'll develop your abilities.

01:07:50.496 --> 01:07:51.872 line:80%
And that was an order, not an offer.

01:07:52.456 --> 01:07:53.832 line:80%
I'm not making excuses, I--

01:07:53.916 --> 01:07:55.292 line:80%
You don't have a choice.

01:07:55.376 --> 01:07:57.836 line:80%
If you really can't do it, then quit.

01:07:57.920 --> 01:08:00.589 line:80%
I raise people for their abilities,
not with sentiment.

01:08:00.673 --> 01:08:01.715 line:80%
I'll give you…

01:08:03.258 --> 01:08:04.510 line:80%
a week for that report.

01:08:04.593 --> 01:08:05.594 line:80%
[sighs]

01:08:10.265 --> 01:08:11.433 line:80%
[sighs heavily]

01:08:12.017 --> 01:08:13.519 line:20%
This is so sudden…

01:08:15.020 --> 01:08:16.021 line:80%
[gasps]

01:08:17.439 --> 01:08:19.525 line:80%
MISSED CALL
ANIMATOR SEONU CHAN

01:08:20.192 --> 01:08:21.193 line:80%
[line connects]

01:08:21.276 --> 01:08:23.988 line:80%
[automation] <i>The number you have dialed</i>
<i>is unavailable. Please leave--</i>

01:08:24.071 --> 01:08:25.698 line:80%
Why is it off?

01:08:27.366 --> 01:08:28.575 line:80%
[sighs]

01:08:29.535 --> 01:08:31.620 line:80%
<i>Call me when you get my message.</i>

01:08:32.371 --> 01:08:33.872 line:80%
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

01:08:33.956 --> 01:08:36.875 line:80%
-[honking]
-[Chan] <i>I couldn't react properly…</i>

01:08:37.459 --> 01:08:39.003 line:80%
Was he driving here?

01:08:41.422 --> 01:08:44.258 line:80%
-Mr. Park, did you hear from Mr. Seonu?
-Oh?

01:08:44.842 --> 01:08:46.927 line:80%
I guess you haven't heard yet.

01:08:48.470 --> 01:08:49.680 line:80%
I got a call.

01:08:51.307 --> 01:08:52.558 line:80%
What call?

01:08:54.184 --> 01:08:56.186 line:80%
[Manjae]
<i>He suddenly had to return to America.</i>

01:08:56.854 --> 01:08:58.897 line:80%
<i>He had to head straight to the airport,</i>

01:08:59.440 --> 01:09:02.192 line:80%
<i>so he asked me to send</i>
<i>his passport through express delivery.</i>

01:09:03.610 --> 01:09:05.571 line:80%
I don't know what's going on, either.

01:09:05.654 --> 01:09:09.616 line:80%
He said he'd call me again soon,
but he hasn't called.

01:09:09.700 --> 01:09:10.701 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

01:09:13.120 --> 01:09:14.121 line:80%
[stutters]

01:09:15.497 --> 01:09:16.623 line:80%
What…

01:09:17.708 --> 01:09:20.044 line:80%
-I…
-[Manjae] He would have left already.

01:09:21.170 --> 01:09:24.798 line:80%
He said he'd take
the earliest flight to the US.

01:09:24.882 --> 01:09:26.967 line:80%
He must be gone already.

01:09:28.635 --> 01:09:29.845 line:80%
[sighs]

01:09:29.928 --> 01:09:31.930 line:80%
[♪ soft emotional song playing]

01:09:41.231 --> 01:09:43.692 line:80%
MISSED CALL
ANIMATOR SEONU CHAN

01:09:47.446 --> 01:09:48.656 line:80%
[sighs softly]

01:09:49.657 --> 01:09:50.866 line:80%
[cell phone buzzes]

01:09:50.949 --> 01:09:52.743 line:80%
YOUR PHOTOS ARE READY FOR PICKUP

01:09:52.826 --> 01:09:53.911 line:80%
HOBAK PHOTO STUDIO

01:10:23.440 --> 01:10:26.026 line:80%
What? He said there were 10 shots.

01:10:27.569 --> 01:10:28.737 line:80%
He was lying. [sighs]

01:10:31.407 --> 01:10:32.408 line:80%
[sighs]

01:10:54.638 --> 01:10:55.639 line:80%
[♪ song ends]

01:10:58.100 --> 01:10:59.560 line:80%
Keep enjoying your life

01:10:59.977 --> 01:11:02.813 line:80%
even when… I'm not here later.

01:11:13.365 --> 01:11:15.367 line:80%
[♪ uplifting song playing]

01:11:24.626 --> 01:11:26.545 line:80%
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:11:50.653 --> 01:11:52.237 line:20%
[Hayeong] <i>They are all gone?</i>

01:11:52.321 --> 01:11:55.407 line:20%
[Haran] <i>What kind of trial ends like this?</i>

01:11:55.491 --> 01:11:58.202 line:20%
-[nurse] Ms. Kim!
-[Manjae] <i>Why did you go to the hospital?</i>

01:11:58.285 --> 01:11:59.828 line:20%
<i>Are you sick?</i>

01:11:59.912 --> 01:12:01.330 line:20%
[Nana] <i>I just want to walk for a bit.</i>

01:12:01.413 --> 01:12:04.041 line:20%
[Hayeong] <i>Chan was such a nice guy.</i>

01:12:04.124 --> 01:12:06.794 line:20%
[Haran] <i>When we first met,</i>

01:12:06.877 --> 01:12:09.505 line:20%
<i>he said I looked like</i>
<i>someone trapped in winter.</i>

01:12:09.588 --> 01:12:12.132 line:20%
[Hayeong] <i>You're not worried about Haran?</i>

01:12:12.216 --> 01:12:13.801 line:20%
[Nana] <i>Do you regret it?</i>

01:12:13.884 --> 01:12:17.137 line:20%
Do you regret getting close to Seonu Chan?

01:12:17.721 --> 01:12:19.598 line:80%
[Haran] <i>Yes, I do.</i>

01:12:23.060 --> 01:12:24.061 line:80%
[♪ song fades]

01:12:24.144 --> 01:12:26.146 line:80%
[♪ theme music playing]

01:12:32.027 --> 01:12:33.028 line:80%
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:12:33.112 --> 01:12:34.113 line:80%
Translated by Juyoung Park